    <node id="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fibrosis qu&#237;stica, also known as cystic fibrosis, is a genetic disorder that primarily affects the lungs and digestive system. It is caused by a mutation in the CFTR gene and is inherited in an autosomal recessive manner. The condition was diagnosed in the patient at the age of 2 and is characterized by a range of complications, including malnutrition and diabetes, which can significantly worsen the patient's prognosis. Due to the complexity of the disease, it necessitates multidisciplinary management and specialized nutritional care to address the various health challenges faced by affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">0977493109f1215441cf1927961d21ee,3f295222427803a7fc92b83386e5ec56,7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab,84e91b50850bfa0ad0122cdebf477a1d,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b</data>
      <data key="d3">4</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">61</data>
      <data key="d7">6b98b0b791c34defb2ae3b4f9af87deb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enfermedad Inflamatoria Intestinal refers to a group of inflammatory conditions affecting the gastrointestinal tract. These conditions may necessitate specific dietary interventions to manage symptoms and improve patient outcomes. Additionally, Enfermedad Inflamatoria Intestinal should be considered in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases, highlighting its relevance in a broader medical context.</data>
      <data key="d2">0977493109f1215441cf1927961d21ee,b8db8cc3349b8ac0cce45497da6244fc</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
