      <data key="d6">62</data>
      <data key="d7">c37d0e7183b340d29441c60cb44b9f1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE CABEZA Y CUELLO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#193;NCER DE CABEZA Y CUELLO refers to a type of cancer that affects the head and neck region. This form of cancer often necessitates nutritional support during treatment due to the challenges it poses in these areas. Specifically, it includes conditions such as carcinoma epidermoide of the hemilangue, which is a type of squamous cell carcinoma that can occur in the oral cavity. Overall, C&#193;NCER DE CABEZA Y CUELLO encompasses various malignancies within the head and neck, highlighting the importance of comprehensive care and support for affected patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">0977493109f1215441cf1927961d21ee,3356667d6f35de6a8587ece00f8c6580</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">63</data>
      <data key="d7">15ddcf8e80eb4d439ea3ffb4f361bdbb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE P&#193;NCREAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#193;NCER DE P&#193;NCREAS is a serious and aggressive form of cancer that affects the pancreas. It is characterized by a low survival rate and is often diagnosed at a late stage due to the absence of early symptoms. Patients diagnosed with this type of cancer require careful nutritional management to support their health and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">0977493109f1215441cf1927961d21ee,a960ccbf15a28151d1461c4203408408</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">64</data>
      <data key="d7">d8b80572286f443db7e58d4c8e0bd32e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL, or enteral nutrition (NE), is a medical method of feeding that delivers nutrients directly into the gastrointestinal tract, bypassing the usual process of eating and digestion. This approach is particularly beneficial for patients who are unable to eat by mouth due to various medical conditions, including swallowing difficulties, severe caloric malnutrition, diabetes, rumination syndrome, and complications following surgery. 

Enteral nutrition is often administered through a nasogastric tube or via a gastrostomy, such as a percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy (PEG), to ensure that patients receive the necessary nutrients when oral intake is insufficient. It is commonly used in the management of conditions like cystic fibrosis and severe acute pancreatitis, where it can improve clinical outcomes and reduce mortality rates. 

The method is preferred over parenteral nutrition in many cases, especially for patients undergoing digestive surgery, as it utilizes the gastrointestinal tract effectively. Overall, enteral nutrition serves as a crucial nutritional support system tailored to meet the specific dietary needs of patients who cannot consume food orally, thereby enhancing their nutritional status and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">0977493109f1215441cf1927961d21ee,1ba0aa1d1330351a62eb6319ffdd30db,234b514a40a64bc02f1346cb62cf3f97,2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315,3a5d7e4dc412f1d4701672c3af3cb4ed,3dfc700a2eaec232c05b0a53f2089229,3f295222427803a7fc92b83386e5ec56,445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce,57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009,5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d,7469cc60475806b519e91abe2796aead,82d36ebbaaa026c713df2b7a47253efa,84e91b50850bfa0ad0122cdebf477a1d,88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe,8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa,9c43759c41fe226a2702de300b9e580a,b7a2c1e4dd77f47605fdb33f4a2c2bdf,bc381304b682e075c7356c6edbfb0c2d,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b,c92ceeeeae88c8288176cbfd00c75e17,ce4c057e0a625bc9e64301a0cca1e206,e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5</data>
      <data key="d3">21</data>
