    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL refers to a medical treatment that delivers nutrition through methods other than traditional eating, making it particularly beneficial for patients who have severe dietary restrictions. This approach is essential for individuals who cannot consume food orally due to various medical conditions. However, it is important to note that artificial nutrition can lead to complications, such as diabetes, especially in patients with specific conditions like MELAS syndrome. Thus, while NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL serves a critical role in patient care, it also necessitates careful management to mitigate potential health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">0977493109f1215441cf1927961d21ee,e3370b71146ad5063d6b1e9c3d8a3bd2</data>
