    <node id="PACIENTE">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">The patient is an individual diagnosed with multiple health conditions, including adenocarcinoma of the pancreas, moderate to severe acute pancreatitis, obesity (grade 1), and type 2 diabetes that was previously controlled. Throughout their medical journey, the patient has experienced a range of symptoms and treatments, including fluctuations in glucose levels and varying insulin requirements. They have also received nutritional support due to complications such as a pancreatic fistula and severe malnutrition.

In addition to these conditions, the patient has been diagnosed with dysphagia secondary to a chronic swallowing disorder post-radiotherapy, leading to moderate caloric-protein malnutrition. They have shown symptoms of rumination syndrome and have undergone multiple treatments to manage this condition. The patient has a history of chronic health issues, including diabetes and liver complications, resulting in significant weight loss over the years.

The patient is a 48-year-old individual with insulin-dependent type 2 diabetes and morbid obesity who underwent gastric bypass surgery. They have also received enteral and parenteral nutrition due to short bowel syndrome and previously undiagnosed diabetes. Post-surgery, the patient faced complications but has shown health improvements with nutritional support through a PEG (percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy).

Additionally, the patient has a history of eating disorders and is currently undergoing evaluation and treatment for both diabetes and these disorders. They are also diagnosed with severe caloric malnutrition, experiencing significant weight loss and gastrointestinal issues, necessitating nutritional intervention via a nasogastric tube. 

The patient is a young woman with Type 1 Diabetes (DM1) and an eating disorder, receiving treatment and monitoring for both conditions. They are also undergoing treatment for a head and neck neoplasm, ischemic stroke, and severe complications related to Crohn's disease, which have involved multiple surgeries and nutritional challenges. Furthermore, the patient has cystic fibrosis and has undergone various nutritional interventions and health monitoring.

Overall, the patient is receiving comprehensive medical care for their complex health issues, including diabetes management, nutritional support, and treatment for various chronic conditions. They are currently being evaluated for metabolic surgery and are experiencing partial remission of diabetes, while also undergoing various nutritional therapies and surgical procedures to address swallowing difficulties and nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c6c9eb4aba5c4642a75d76bd7ea08ba,1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec,17b7995dcf275c50629c7e3d4723882e,3f295222427803a7fc92b83386e5ec56,3f685a05a9682db6dcde958d1918cc77,445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce,449d46789f604265753884e2d371ec8c,4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a,48f1fe343d54cd0f353be34b736a352c,49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40,4b4f297dec86d7f65e362ad688bbb28f,514518b96e32b025815b45cc2a504f0d,59fd1772b0c4b6c23c975977be6a60fe,5cf8b1c5491f78fda9bca97f3d14c5a2,67f96f3e5c366f82de31f1bf189aa71f,763c8ac63b4c91616bcea6f1f4aa38c9,7c10030e29c1434df3b10b1533710486,7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab,82d36ebbaaa026c713df2b7a47253efa,83b82871866963bb43f901dd9ca09fcb,933d6526b2d313c95c9f4aaa950a62a3,9c43759c41fe226a2702de300b9e580a,a5ee3f91f8571820c338a8db4d3db09d,acd36e6dbcd98757c4cf33ff090764ee,b00c312f46e790b32fe99743480f9e47,b7a2c1e4dd77f47605fdb33f4a2c2bdf,bc381304b682e075c7356c6edbfb0c2d,bfdbf41efa08067d5ae1b1a67830affd,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b,c92ceeeeae88c8288176cbfd00c75e17,ce4c057e0a625bc9e64301a0cca1e206,da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc,e70fa2e099766154321f13c0112d436a,e7df0ed14559db764d393fb9411fec33,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5,efe29025266e1689abb9b0a2783e5ea3</data>
