      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">83</data>
      <data key="d7">9736c8dec8e946be940f87f15053894f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SPAIN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Spain is a country located in Southern Europe, recognized for its significant public health challenges, particularly concerning the increasing prevalence of diabetes mellitus. It ranks fourth in Europe for the number of individuals affected by diabetes, highlighting the urgency of addressing this health issue. Various studies have been conducted in Spain to explore diabetes prevalence and management, including a notable study by Olveira et al. that focused on enteral nutrition and diabetes in hospitalized patients. Additionally, Spain is the site of the PREDYCES study, which estimates the costs associated with disease-related malnutrition. Overall, Spain's health landscape is marked by a critical need for effective diabetes management and nutritional interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ba0aa1d1330351a62eb6319ffdd30db,3defb74705676a025b15398e300eb230,45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d,d52ef4e5955918a8a47b697fcdb4096f,dec6b3fc008edd47758cfc00106d077b</data>
      <data key="d3">19</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">84</data>
      <data key="d7">7e77959cdd7a417e936231976b17f091</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL ESPECIALIZADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Specialized nutritional support refers to medical nutritional therapy that includes oral nutritional supplements, enteral nutrition, and parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d</data>
      <data key="d3">19</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">85</data>
      <data key="d7">2dede70ac24a4eb6a3b0c28c1676f9b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SNO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SNO refers to oral nutritional supplements designed to support the dietary needs of patients, particularly those at risk of malnutrition. These specialized nutritional supplements are administered orally and are particularly beneficial for patients with malnutrition, those preparing for surgery, and individuals managing diabetes. SNO encompasses a range of nutritional formulas tailored to enhance dietary intake, providing essential calories and nutrients necessary for recovery and overall health. Additionally, SNO includes specific nutritional support for patients undergoing cancer treatment, ensuring that their unique dietary requirements are met. Overall, SNO plays a crucial role in improving the nutritional status of patients in various medical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">3a5d7e4dc412f1d4701672c3af3cb4ed,3ed179f6e734d9fe4921fb0be0b018e4,45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d,49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40,5aa4da1a8d1e0b60ec7e801c7db1701c,acd36e6dbcd98757c4cf33ff090764ee,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3,dc7539b4d637d6dd09963c2564f4f084</data>
      <data key="d3">19</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">86</data>
      <data key="d7">eab423303c684ac98cdfb1482e7d0b6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALNUTRICI&#211;N RELACIONADA CON LA ENFERMEDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MALNUTRICI&#211;N RELACIONADA CON LA ENFERMEDAD, also known as disease-related malnutrition (DRE), is a condition characterized by a compromised nutritional status in patients due to illness. This condition significantly impacts clinical outcomes and contributes to increased healthcare costs. DRE is recognized as a major public health issue, particularly in developed countries, where it is associated with heightened risks of morbidity and mortality.</data>
      <data key="d2">45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d,c55f34a09dbf07224c85384f08173e27</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">87</data>
      <data key="d7">128b84ef3f6f4a85b32ea46c04bdb742</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES GERI&#193;TRICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Geriatric patients are a specific group particularly affected by disease-related malnutrition, as highlighted in the PREDYCES study.</data>
      <data key="d2">45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">88</data>
      <data key="d7">cc8c231986a442b9b6e769472b4c0c6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES ONCOL&#211;GICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Oncological patients are another group at high risk for disease-related malnutrition, as indicated by the findings of the PREDYCES study.</data>
      <data key="d2">45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">89</data>
      <data key="d7">ac11e981a1c34a91bfaf9feb9b759605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMOS MAYORES DE 70 A&#209;OS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Patients over 70 years old are significantly affected by disease-related malnutrition, with a prevalence of 37% according to the PREDYCES study.</data>
      <data key="d2">45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">90</data>
      <data key="d7">1fbe71db9103492e876c19549437cf71</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISFAGIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Disfagia, also known as dysphagia, is a medical condition characterized by difficulty swallowing. This condition can lead to various complications, including an increased risk of disease-related malnutrition, which affects a significant portion of hospitalized patients. In one particular case, a patient experienced disfagia, prompting a referral to the ORL (Otorhinolaryngology) department for further evaluation and management.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d,9c43759c41fe226a2702de300b9e580a</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">91</data>
      <data key="d7">912fa5c609e1439b9b7a305f145e24d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLIMEDICACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polypharmacy is a risk factor for disease-related malnutrition, particularly in elderly and complex chronic patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">92</data>
      <data key="d7">7a370aa38d81490485a80dd2a009c8cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NOURISH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The NOURISH study is a recent multicenter clinical trial examining the effects of a hyperproteic nutritional supplement enriched with beta-hydroxy-beta-methylbutyrate on malnourished elderly patients in hospitals.</data>
      <data key="d2">c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471</data>
      <data key="d3">11</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">93</data>
      <data key="d7">3c3d781efbef4075b61d31d8ad2b09c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESPEN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ESPEN, or the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism, is a professional organization dedicated to providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for nutritional support across various patient populations. It focuses on patients with specific health conditions, including those with dementia, oncology patients, elderly individuals, and those with polymorbid conditions. ESPEN emphasizes the importance of nutritional screening, assessment, and treatment, advocating for the use of oral nutritional supplements (ONS) to enhance dietary intake and mitigate complications. Additionally, the organization addresses the nutritional needs of patients with intestinal issues and provides guidance on clinical nutrition and hydration, which is particularly relevant for diabetes management. Through its efforts, ESPEN aims to improve the overall nutritional care and outcomes for patients facing diverse health challenges.</data>
      <data key="d2">242881af1a0439ab16c10b788cff01fd,5aa4da1a8d1e0b60ec7e801c7db1701c,5cf8b1c5491f78fda9bca97f3d14c5a2,76c4ef07f382585bf943bfaf57372c86,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3,c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471,dec6b3fc008edd47758cfc00106d077b</data>
      <data key="d3">11</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">94</data>
      <data key="d7">f5596d5a8f764010a9015de9f4d20f60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHILIPSON ET AL.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Philipson et al. conducted an analysis of hospital admission records of 44 million hospitalized patients in the U.S. over 11 years, focusing on the impact of oral nutritional supplements on hospital stays and readmission rates.</data>
      <data key="d2">c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471</data>
      <data key="d3">11</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">95</data>
      <data key="d7">0068953b652e46c0a15bfc8d8ec03a3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELIA ET AL.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Elia et al. published systematic reviews and meta-analyses regarding the use of oral nutritional supplements in hospitalized and community patients with various pathologies.</data>
      <data key="d2">c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471</data>
      <data key="d3">11</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">96</data>
      <data key="d7">6c1aacdafda9457e9551090788876411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BALLY ET AL.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Bally et al. conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on nutritional support and outcomes in malnourished medical inpatients.</data>
      <data key="d2">c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471</data>
      <data key="d3">11</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">97</data>
      <data key="d7">d430b6bc46ba4b88a5e0682502c15ccc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITALIZATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospitalization refers to the process of admitting a patient to a hospital for medical care and treatment. It encompasses the admission of patients for various types of medical interventions, and is a key context in which the benefits of oral nutritional supplements are evaluated.</data>
      <data key="d2">178140d0d29364593546d7d21393f2c6,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451,c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471</data>
      <data key="d3">22</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">98</data>
      <data key="d7">a4e8d07bb6e2415db815fd3b5a54e57c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALNOURISHED PATIENTS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Malnourished patients are individuals who are hospitalized and at risk of complications due to inadequate nutritional intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471</data>
      <data key="d3">11</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">99</data>
      <data key="d7">8397aa02a91f4f499456ec2070765447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITAL READMISSIONS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospital readmissions refer to the instances when patients return to the hospital after discharge, which is a key metric evaluated in studies regarding the effectiveness of nutritional supplements.</data>
      <data key="d2">c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471</data>
      <data key="d3">11</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">100</data>
      <data key="d7">ac7ab93d0a434e178b7dee1ef2c0f91c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional support encompasses a range of interventions designed to enhance dietary intake and improve health outcomes for patients. This practice includes the use of oral nutritional supplements and other dietary interventions aimed at managing health conditions and improving nutritional status. It is particularly important for patients who are unable to meet their nutritional needs through regular eating, such as those with complications from conditions like obesity or diabetes. Overall, nutritional support plays a crucial role in providing dietary assistance to individuals in need, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients to support their health and recovery.</data>
      <data key="d2">178140d0d29364593546d7d21393f2c6,242881af1a0439ab16c10b788cff01fd,58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88,6edff59a3b151e946e7664f13bcb0931,c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471</data>
      <data key="d3">11</data>
