    </node>
    <node id="SEEN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The SEEN is the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition, focusing on diabetes and nutrition-related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">dec6b3fc008edd47758cfc00106d077b</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">104</data>
      <data key="d7">c50b3d35c366488698a24a00467bd5e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CASTILLA Y LE&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Castilla y Le&#243;n is an autonomous community in Spain that is experiencing a notable increase in the prevalence of diabetes and related mortality rates. This region is characterized by an aging population, which contributes to the growing health concern surrounding diabetes. In response to this public health issue, clinical case conferences have been held in Castilla y Le&#243;n to address and discuss the challenges posed by diabetes in the community. Overall, diabetes remains a significant health concern in Castilla y Le&#243;n, highlighting the need for ongoing attention and intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">7949b821c1ca2e4adc524e7775626396,d2e2009d967ecd49af312dba4e2ed4fd,dec6b3fc008edd47758cfc00106d077b,fc8df7c3d7a0d2286c55493077ed3937</data>
      <data key="d3">14</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">105</data>
      <data key="d7">afc8a1df6c804079a52a24dc73c513cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IDF">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The International Diabetes Federation (IDF) is an organization dedicated to providing data and advocacy related to diabetes on a global scale. It plays a crucial role in raising awareness and promoting education about diabetes through its various initiatives. One of its key contributions is the publication of the Atlas of Diabetes, which offers comprehensive global epidemiological data on the prevalence and impact of diabetes worldwide. Through these efforts, the IDF aims to improve the understanding of diabetes and support efforts to combat this growing health issue.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2e2009d967ecd49af312dba4e2ed4fd,dec6b3fc008edd47758cfc00106d077b</data>
      <data key="d3">14</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">106</data>
      <data key="d7">fd8d8071ae014bf5b256e31b7f72e52b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XXIX CONGRESO NACIONAL DE LA SOCIEDAD ESPA&#209;OLA DE DIABETES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The XXIX National Congress of the Spanish Diabetes Society is a significant event focused on diabetes research and awareness. During this congress, the results of the di@bet.es study were presented, highlighting important findings related to diabetes management and care. Additionally, the congress served as a platform for presenting new data on the prevalence of diabetes in Spain, contributing to the understanding of the disease's impact within the country. This event underscores the ongoing efforts of the Spanish Diabetes Society to advance knowledge and improve outcomes for individuals affected by diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">ac8c5a07bd415723c0410ec34b9d7c5e,dec6b3fc008edd47758cfc00106d077b</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
