      <data key="d7">ab344aab71db4afeae4abeaaf856528f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORTALIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MORTALIDAD refers to the rate of deaths in patients with acute pancreatitis, which can be influenced by the type of nutritional support provided. Additionally, mortality related to diabetes is a significant public health concern, as diabetes is one of the leading causes of death in Western countries. The increased risk of death associated with diabetes has been emphasized by various studies and statistics, highlighting the serious implications of this condition on overall mortality rates.</data>
      <data key="d2">5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d,ac8c5a07bd415723c0410ec34b9d7c5e,fc8df7c3d7a0d2286c55493077ed3937</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">115</data>
      <data key="d7">57e4168a839a45779d2d608bde6c80ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POBLACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The population refers to the general public in Castilla y Le&#243;n, particularly those affected by diabetes and its related health issues.</data>
