    <node id="DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is a prevalent form of diabetes characterized by insulin resistance, significantly impacting health interventions. It is a major health concern in Spain, with a prevalence rate of 13.8% in the general population and an incidence of 11.58 cases per 1000 people per year. This chronic condition affects how the body metabolizes glucose, leading to increased mortality risk, particularly in regions such as Castilla y Le&#243;n.

Patients with Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 often manage the condition over many years; for instance, one patient has been managing it for 15 years, while another has been managing it for 10 years. In some cases, the condition is insulin-dependent and poorly controlled. Despite these challenges, there are instances where the diabetes was well-controlled prior to hospitalization, and some patients have undergone surgical interventions related to their diabetes management.

Additionally, there is a familial aspect to Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2, as indicated by a family history of the disease, such as a diagnosis in the patient's grandmother. Overall, Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is a chronic metabolic disease that requires ongoing management and can lead to serious health complications if not properly controlled.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,2f91f92c99da813a8d1be2f6ac0fa552,319591d16b552cff77a5cd56e69c1ca2,3356667d6f35de6a8587ece00f8c6580,410fab643c125e0f8944ebae5dba5ec0,449d46789f604265753884e2d371ec8c,4b4f297dec86d7f65e362ad688bbb28f,7949b821c1ca2e4adc524e7775626396,ac8c5a07bd415723c0410ec34b9d7c5e,d2e2009d967ecd49af312dba4e2ed4fd,da2707b26ddb548995a6d0e2a3eeddb0,e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849,e70fa2e099766154321f13c0112d436a,efe29025266e1689abb9b0a2783e5ea3</data>
