    <node id="OMS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The OMS, or World Health Organization (WHO), is a specialized agency of the United Nations dedicated to international public health. It plays a crucial role in providing data on various health issues, including the prevalence of diabetes worldwide. Additionally, the WHO is responsible for establishing guidelines for the classification of diseases, thereby contributing to global health standards and practices.</data>
