    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES TIPO 2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes tipo 2 is a chronic medical condition that has affected the patient for 12 years, primarily linked to obesity and challenges in glucose control. This form of diabetes is characterized by insulin resistance and is often associated with lifestyle factors, making it a significant health concern. It is prevalent in Spain and has implications for healthcare resources and costs. The increasing prevalence of diabetes tipo 2, particularly among older populations, highlights the need for effective management strategies, including the recommendation of metabolic surgery for obese patients. Overall, diabetes tipo 2 represents a major public health issue that requires ongoing attention and intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">201f8e6a0d6c49396cf9c81f5da4520f,39ea441f219d949e8bc3c6f430970689,445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce,a549bdc3929c5dd7a613c6900a0fe90e,f2846d08229fda837153207946e29831</data>
