    <node id="MNA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The MNA, or Mini Nutritional Assessment, is a validated method designed for nutritional screening in individuals over the age of 65. It serves as a crucial tool for evaluating the risk of malnutrition among various patient populations, including those with diabetes. This comprehensive assessment helps identify nutritional deficiencies and supports the development of appropriate interventions to improve the health and well-being of older adults.</data>
