    <node id="HOSPITAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The hospital is a comprehensive healthcare institution that provides a wide range of medical services and treatments to patients. It is where individuals receive medical attention for various conditions, including consultations in endocrinology and nutrition, as well as surgical and medical treatments. The hospital plays a crucial role in the management of serious illnesses, such as adenocarcinoma of the pancreas, where it facilitates patient admissions and palliative care. Additionally, it offers specialized care for patients with neurodegenerative diseases, including Alzheimer's, and supports those with metabolic disorders like diabetes and malnutrition. The hospital is also equipped to provide multidisciplinary care for patients with Mitochondrial Neurogastrointestinal Encephalomyopathy (MNGIE), which includes nutritional support and evaluations for potential transplants. Furthermore, it serves as a critical facility for urgent medical situations, such as the evaluation and treatment of strokes, ensuring that patients receive timely and appropriate care for their conditions. Overall, the hospital is a vital institution dedicated to the health and well-being of its patients through a variety of medical services and treatments.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c6c9eb4aba5c4642a75d76bd7ea08ba,1ba0aa1d1330351a62eb6319ffdd30db,2f91f92c99da813a8d1be2f6ac0fa552,763c8ac63b4c91616bcea6f1f4aa38c9,76c4ef07f382585bf943bfaf57372c86,83b82871866963bb43f901dd9ca09fcb,acd36e6dbcd98757c4cf33ff090764ee</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
