    </node>
    <node id="CIBERDEM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">CIBERDEM, officially known as the Centro de Investigaci&#243;n Biom&#233;dica en Red de Diabetes y Enfermedades Metab&#243;licas Asociadas, is a prominent biomedical research center dedicated to the study of diabetes and associated metabolic diseases. This center has conducted significant research, including a study on the incidence of diabetes in Spain, highlighting its commitment to understanding and addressing the challenges posed by these health issues. CIBERDEM plays a crucial role in advancing knowledge and developing solutions related to diabetes and its related conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">3defb74705676a025b15398e300eb230,ac8c5a07bd415723c0410ec34b9d7c5e</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">238</data>
      <data key="d7">792d7faf00ba44f2895dcb18952af42d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DARIOS STUDY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The DARIOS study is a research project that reviewed multiple studies on cardiovascular risk factors in Spain, revealing a diabetes prevalence of 13%.</data>
      <data key="d2">3defb74705676a025b15398e300eb230</data>
      <data key="d3">19</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">239</data>
      <data key="d7">efd3a4dbff2146df88c560855edd3ca5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DI@BET STUDY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Di@bet study was conducted between 2008 and 2010, assessing diabetes prevalence among the Spanish population, finding a 13.8% prevalence rate.</data>
      <data key="d2">3defb74705676a025b15398e300eb230</data>
      <data key="d3">19</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">240</data>
      <data key="d7">a17ecb6ec27241d98f9b2b1343bd2bab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OVIEDO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Oviedo is the capital city of the province of Asturias in Spain, where the Hospital Universitario Central de Asturias is located.</data>
      <data key="d2">3defb74705676a025b15398e300eb230</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">241</data>
      <data key="d7">bb8eec9d2a0149bebce619b3a01acfdb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES MELLITUS TYPE 2">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">3defb74705676a025b15398e300eb230</data>
      <data key="d3">19</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">242</data>
      <data key="d7">0c4a85094f3340c5854e0c9d8cb878e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESPA&#209;A">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Spain is a country that faces significant health challenges, particularly concerning its youth. Nearly 30,000 minors under the age of 15 are affected by Diabetes Mellitus Type 1. Additionally, Spain has reported notable prevalence rates of eating disorders among its population. The country has also been the focus of studies on diabetes incidence, which have revealed alarming prevalence rates, highlighting the urgent need for attention to these health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">ac8c5a07bd415723c0410ec34b9d7c5e,bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">14</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">243</data>
      <data key="d7">9e209d349df1451a844e7d04027faf64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SECCAID">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SECCAID is a study that assessed the direct annual costs of diabetes in Spain.</data>
      <data key="d2">ac8c5a07bd415723c0410ec34b9d7c5e</data>
      <data key="d3">14</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">244</data>
      <data key="d7">d5e325d32e254c9a86262dee7bc57140</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERTENSION ARTERIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypertension is a risk factor associated with diabetes that increases the risk of cardiovascular diseases.</data>
      <data key="d2">ac8c5a07bd415723c0410ec34b9d7c5e</data>
      <data key="d3">14</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
