    <node id="MESA REDONDA DE CASOS CL&#205;NICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "MESA REDONDA DE CASOS CL&#205;NICOS" is a round table event focused on discussing clinical cases within the medical community. It features various medical professionals who present and analyze different cases. The event has taken place in the Comunidad Valenciana, where a diverse group of specialists share their insights. Additionally, there is a specific iteration of this event that addresses clinical cases related to diabetes and nutrition, which was held in Granada, also involving various specialists. Overall, the MESA REDONDA DE CASOS CL&#205;NICOS serves as a platform for collaboration and knowledge exchange among healthcare professionals across different regions and specialties.</data>
      <data key="d2">234b514a40a64bc02f1346cb62cf3f97,a86e44ac34c096cea172895339d5f733</data>
      <data key="d3">6</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">287</data>
      <data key="d7">78b5a505fef64c9b917e81455abeae42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME MELAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A rare genetic disorder discussed in one of the clinical cases, characterized by mitochondrial dysfunction and associated with diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">a86e44ac34c096cea172895339d5f733</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">288</data>
      <data key="d7">0b6de396ea574687a930e3302dbf7fd4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OBESIDAD M&#211;RBIDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"OBESIDAD M&#211;RBIDA" refers to a medical condition characterized by severe obesity, which poses significant health risks and complications. This condition has been discussed in clinical cases, highlighting its impact on patients who often experience multiple attempts at weight loss and may ultimately require surgical intervention, such as bariatric surgery. Morbid obesity is particularly resistant to conventional treatment methods and is associated with an increased risk of serious health issues, including diabetes and pancreatic cancer. Overall, "obesidad m&#243;rbida" represents a critical health concern that necessitates comprehensive management and intervention strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">39ea441f219d949e8bc3c6f430970689,67f96f3e5c366f82de31f1bf189aa71f,8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa,a86e44ac34c096cea172895339d5f733,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3,e70fa2e099766154321f13c0112d436a,efe29025266e1689abb9b0a2783e5ea3</data>
      <data key="d3">14</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">289</data>
      <data key="d7">537a5a8f9d1345e983f3180929b0f3c6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEOPLASIA INTRADUCTAL PAPILAR MUCINOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neoplasia intraductal papilar mucinosa is a specific type of pancreatic tumor that has been discussed in clinical cases. It is associated with malnutrition and diabetes, highlighting its potential impact on the patient's overall health. The patient in the case was diagnosed with this type of tumor, indicating its clinical significance and the need for careful management of related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944,a86e44ac34c096cea172895339d5f733</data>
      <data key="d3">21</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">290</data>
      <data key="d7">72d2d6a0987543219bfdb4f91ce28e7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO SANTA LUC&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospital General Universitario Santa Luc&#237;a is a healthcare institution in Cartagena where specialized medical care is provided, including for patients with endocrine and nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">291</data>
      <data key="d7">d57004e51dd34612a4806032dd9a7267</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE MELAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MELAS is a mitochondrial disease characterized by encephalomyopathy, lactic acidosis, and stroke-like episodes, significantly affecting muscle and nervous system function, often leading to complications such as diabetes mellitus.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">292</data>
      <data key="d7">29f317181826412bb0c0f6dab8fca52c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIRUG&#205;A BARI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CIRUG&#205;A BARI&#193;TRICA refers to a medical procedure increasingly utilized to address obesity, particularly among diabetic patients. This surgical intervention is designed to assist individuals suffering from obesity in losing weight and managing associated health complications, including type 2 diabetes. Specifically, bariatric surgery is often performed as an elective procedure for patients with morbid obesity, with one common method being a simplified gastric bypass. While the procedure is associated with low complication rates, it is important to note that the risks may increase with additional interventions. Overall, CIRUG&#205;A BARI&#193;TRICA serves as a significant option for improving health outcomes in individuals struggling with severe obesity.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315,39ea441f219d949e8bc3c6f430970689,67f96f3e5c366f82de31f1bf189aa71f,8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa,efe29025266e1689abb9b0a2783e5ea3</data>
      <data key="d3">14</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">293</data>
      <data key="d7">4baf8d6272c749bcbaf545622ad539ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES MITOCONDRIALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mitochondrial diseases are a group of disorders caused by dysfunctional mitochondria, which can lead to a variety of health issues, including metabolic and neurological problems.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">294</data>
      <data key="d7">6b1bce34447c4f18a214642747c88dfa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALNUTRICI&#211;N CAL&#211;RICA SEVERA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Severe caloric malnutrition is a condition resulting from inadequate intake of calories, leading to significant health issues, particularly in patients with complex medical conditions like MELAS.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">295</data>
      <data key="d7">e299686b3ac04b649ea08330c84df189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLINEUROPAT&#205;A SENSITIVO-MOTORA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">POLINEUROPAT&#205;A SENSITIVO-MOTORA, also known as sensory-motor polyneuropathy, is a medical condition that impacts the peripheral nerves. This condition is characterized by both sensory loss and motor weakness, which can significantly affect a patient's quality of life. It is often observed in individuals with mitochondrial diseases, highlighting a potential link between these two health issues. Overall, sensory-motor polyneuropathy represents a serious neurological disorder that requires careful management and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88,8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">296</data>
      <data key="d7">524e5182efd0409388b048ca98a9c9a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DUODENOPANCREATECTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Duodenopancreatectomy is a surgical procedure involving the removal of the duodenum and pancreas, often performed in cases of pancreatic cancer, which can lead to complications such as diabetes and malabsorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">297</data>
      <data key="d7">7a42597256374fba8f86200465946ce0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOMA MUCINOSO DE P&#193;NCREAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mucinous pancreatic carcinoma is a type of cancer that affects the pancreas, characterized by the production of mucin, and may require surgical intervention like duodenopancreatectomy.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">298</data>
      <data key="d7">d427e7205a02457793221ff8a9c0ab49</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MELAS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">MELAS, which stands for Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes, is the most common mitochondrial disease. It is characterized by a heterogeneous phenotypic expression that includes a variety of symptoms affecting multiple systems in the body. Individuals with MELAS often experience neurological impairments, such as migraines, seizures, and episodes resembling strokes. Additionally, the disorder can lead to muscular weakness and various gastrointestinal issues, which frequently result in malnutrition. Other systemic manifestations may include diabetes mellitus. The complexity of MELAS symptoms can vary significantly among affected individuals, making diagnosis and management challenging. One patient was diagnosed with MELAS in 2008, highlighting the ongoing recognition and understanding of this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">59fd1772b0c4b6c23c975977be6a60fe,6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0,e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">26</data>
      <data key="d6">299</data>
      <data key="d7">b520c93bcfba44c29f056516f8f9d534</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARGININA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Arginina is an amino acid that plays a crucial role in the production of nitric oxide (NO), a compound essential for vascular relaxation. It is considered a therapeutic agent that may enhance the availability of nitric oxide, potentially aiding in the treatment of symptoms associated with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes). Through its involvement in nitric oxide synthesis, Arginina is linked to the underlying pathology of MELAS, suggesting its importance in managing this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">300</data>
      <data key="d7">cfedf4a7e7fb40508f06f125d56f7d47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CITRULINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Citrulina is an amino acid supplement known for its role in increasing the production of nitric oxide (NO) in the body. It is considered to have better absorption and bioavailability compared to arginine, another amino acid. While Citrulina is relevant in the context of MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes), particularly for patients who exhibit low levels of nitric oxide, its specific effects on this condition have not been thoroughly studied.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">301</data>
      <data key="d7">fe306d1aa79c424cb745bfa224e59ee1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CITOCROMO C">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Citocromo C is an enzyme that has a high affinity for nitric oxide and is implicated in the pathophysiology of MELAS due to its interaction with nitric oxide synthase.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">302</data>
      <data key="d7">41c5f7f6ca594a288aa404b567c9032b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDOSIS L&#193;CTICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acidosis l&#225;ctica is a prevalent condition observed in patients with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes). It arises due to mitochondrial dysfunction, which is a hallmark of the syndrome. This metabolic disturbance is characterized by an accumulation of lactic acid in the body, and it is recognized as a diagnostic criterion for MELAS.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">303</data>
      <data key="d7">76275e761e894676ad2b4ee6ad26a82d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EPILESIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Epilepsy is a neurological manifestation observed in a significant percentage of MELAS patients, contributing to the overall clinical picture of the syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">304</data>
      <data key="d7">aa5b1bd5350d4892b81bd742fe865c62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROPAT&#205;A PERIF&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neuropat&#237;a perif&#233;rica is a condition affecting the peripheral nerves, noted in MELAS patients, contributing to their neurological symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">305</data>
      <data key="d7">7a6aacb12315475b9f070a9b812e4a8b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#211;XIDO N&#205;TRICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">&#211;xido n&#237;trico is a signaling molecule that plays a critical role in vascular relaxation and is implicated in the pathophysiology of MELAS due to its interaction with endothelial cells.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">306</data>
      <data key="d7">41b1b00b0b0b4e6991299e4cb46e7fd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CITOCROMO C OXIDASA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Citocromo C oxidasa is an enzyme that is involved in the electron transport chain and is noted for its increased activity in MELAS patients, affecting nitric oxide availability.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">307</data>
      <data key="d7">60db37951e044589a65338b58bc5e5ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOACUSIA NEUROSENSORIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipoacusia neurosensorial is a type of hearing loss that is commonly observed in patients with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes). This auditory manifestation significantly contributes to the overall neurological symptoms associated with the syndrome, thereby affecting the quality of life of those affected. Additionally, it is noted that hipoacusia neurosensorial can also be experienced by family members, such as the patient's mother, indicating a potential genetic link related to the underlying mutation.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0,e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">308</data>
      <data key="d7">825c4b54d77849c8aa995ef1986c6838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEMANDA DE INSULINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Demanda de insulina refers to the requirement for insulin treatment in MELAS patients, particularly in those developing diabetes mellitus.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">309</data>
      <data key="d7">41c1946e61d14d30ac13106dbafa5d3d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEW CASTLE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">New Castle is associated with the scale of severity for adult mitochondrial diseases, specifically the NMDAS used to assess patients with MELAS.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">310</data>
      <data key="d7">17a4a9e49d3d4dadaed429135cf042cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COENZIMA Q10">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Coenzima Q10 is a compound that stabilizes the electron transport chain and has antioxidant properties, potentially benefiting patients with MELAS.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">311</data>
      <data key="d7">c359c07cf31a475383dba774c61f7031</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IMC">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The &#205;ndice de Masa Corporal (IMC), or Body Mass Index (BMI), is a critical measure used to assess body weight in relation to height, which is essential for evaluating the nutritional status of individuals. It serves as a tool for classifying obesity and identifying malnutrition risks. For instance, one patient exhibited an IMC of 16 kg/m&#178;, indicating a low weight for their height of 1.75 m, while another patient had an IMC of 36.2 kg/m&#178; at discharge and a subsequent IMC of 29.44 kg/m&#178; during a follow-up review, reflecting a significant change in their nutritional status over time. Generally, an IMC value below 20 kg/m&#178; is associated with a risk of malnutrition, highlighting the importance of monitoring this index in clinical settings. Overall, the IMC is a vital metric for understanding and managing patients' health concerning their weight and height.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce,82d36ebbaaa026c713df2b7a47253efa,8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0,dc7539b4d637d6dd09963c2564f4f084,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5,efe29025266e1689abb9b0a2783e5ea3</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">312</data>
      <data key="d7">763ca956254c4b0fa49d553fbb3e0e95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NTOMAS GASTROINTESTINALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">S&#237;ntomas gastrointestinales refer to digestive symptoms that increase the risk of malnutrition in patients with MELAS.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">313</data>
      <data key="d7">6b478e46c95c4c49bf502050c9f6f41c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA CETOG&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Dieta cetog&#233;nica is a dietary approach that may reduce epileptic seizures in MELAS patients, although its long-term safety and effectiveness are unknown.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">314</data>
      <data key="d7">210b5e8a4d9144a9a37d2ec76cc7bd7d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EPILEPSIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Epilepsia is a neurological manifestation that occurs in a significant percentage of MELAS patients, contributing to their overall health challenges.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">315</data>
      <data key="d7">516d9bdfde044007b2cd75105680ea26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEMANCIAS PSIQUI&#193;TRICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Demanias psiqui&#225;tricas refer to psychiatric manifestations that may arise in patients with MELAS, impacting their mental health.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">316</data>
      <data key="d7">e7034f91c10046ee97fdad348dab84be</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIOTOP&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Miopat&#237;a is a cardinal manifestation of MELAS, characterized by muscle weakness and intolerance to exercise.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">317</data>
      <data key="d7">74edf82098204238b80137d46d363fb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIOCARDIOPAT&#205;A HIPERTR&#211;FICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Miocardiopat&#237;a hipertr&#243;fica is a cardiac manifestation that can occur in MELAS patients, affecting heart function.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">318</data>
      <data key="d7">43964b159dd64dd39056be1c4a3e0b31</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TALLA BAJA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Talla baja refers to short stature, which can be a manifestation in MELAS patients due to hormonal deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
