    <node id="PATIENT">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The patient encompasses a diverse group of individuals with varying health conditions. One notable case is a 29-year-old woman diagnosed with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes), who is experiencing multiple neurological and gastrointestinal symptoms, necessitating chronic treatment. Additionally, there is a 76-year-old male patient suffering from type 2 diabetes and moderate to severe malnutrition, who requires specialized nutritional support and careful monitoring. Furthermore, the patient is also described as an individual undergoing nutritional assessment and treatment specifically for diabetes and malnutrition. Lastly, another aspect of the patient includes an individual with an oncological condition, specifically a neuroendocrine tumor of the pancreas, who requires various types of nutritional support throughout their treatment. Collectively, these descriptions highlight the complex and multifaceted health needs of patients dealing with chronic illnesses, nutritional deficiencies, and oncological conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">6edff59a3b151e946e7664f13bcb0931,7a6970183393c5ef1adc99851ef3eada,84e91b50850bfa0ad0122cdebf477a1d,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451,e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5</data>
