    <node id="SNG">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SNG, or nasogastric tube, is a medical device utilized for feeding and medication administration in patients who have difficulties swallowing or cannot safely consume food orally. It serves as a method of nutritional support, specifically designed for enteral feeding. The nasogastric tube is essential for providing nutrition to patients who require assistance due to various medical conditions. In Spanish, SNG is referred to as "sonda nasog&#225;strica," emphasizing its role in enteral nutrition for patients. Overall, SNG is a critical tool in the management of patients needing dietary support through alternative means.</data>
      <data key="d2">242881af1a0439ab16c10b788cff01fd,5cf8b1c5491f78fda9bca97f3d14c5a2,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451,b7a2c1e4dd77f47605fdb33f4a2c2bdf,e7df0ed14559db764d393fb9411fec33</data>
