      <data key="d6">346</data>
      <data key="d7">40cadc2d50a94ea18274901a99a018d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITALIZACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospitalizaci&#243;n refers to the process of admitting a patient to a hospital for medical treatment. This may be necessary for various conditions, including head and neck cancers, where patients may require a period of hospitalization for their treatment. Additionally, hospitalizaci&#243;n can also be essential in cases such as acute pancreatitis, where patients need specialized care. Furthermore, the hospitalization process may involve monitoring and treating severe malnutrition and its related complications, ensuring that patients receive comprehensive medical attention during their stay.</data>
      <data key="d2">449d46789f604265753884e2d371ec8c,5aa4da1a8d1e0b60ec7e801c7db1701c,88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e,b7a2c1e4dd77f47605fdb33f4a2c2bdf</data>
