    <node id="INSULINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Insulina is a crucial hormone used in the management of diabetes, particularly Type 1 diabetes. It plays a vital role in regulating blood glucose levels, which is essential for the health of patients, including those with additional conditions such as pancreatic cancer. The patient has been receiving insulin treatment as part of their diabetes management, with adjustments made to both basal and corrective insulin guidelines to optimize their blood sugar control. 

Despite the importance of insulin therapy, the patient has been omitting doses, which can adversely affect their blood sugar management. Insulin levels have been closely monitored and adjusted following the patient's diabetes diagnosis to ensure effective treatment. The administration of insulin is tailored to the patient's needs, with different regimens employed to maintain stable glucose levels. Overall, insulina is integral to the patient's treatment plan, influencing not only their diabetes management but also their overall nutritional status and health.</data>
      <data key="d2">3a1d1c4eb34995d440bd72c4b64e3c8d,3ed179f6e734d9fe4921fb0be0b018e4,410fab643c125e0f8944ebae5dba5ec0,48f1fe343d54cd0f353be34b736a352c,7c10030e29c1434df3b10b1533710486,83b82871866963bb43f901dd9ca09fcb,88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e,933d6526b2d313c95c9f4aaa950a62a3,b00c312f46e790b32fe99743480f9e47,b7a2c1e4dd77f47605fdb33f4a2c2bdf,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3,ce4c057e0a625bc9e64301a0cca1e206,dc7539b4d637d6dd09963c2564f4f084</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
