    </node>
    <node id="PEG">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PEG, or percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy, is a medical procedure designed to facilitate nutrition for patients who are unable to adequately feed themselves orally. This method provides long-term nutritional support and is particularly useful in managing the nutritional needs of patients with specific medical conditions, such as diabetes and MELAS syndrome. The procedure involves the placement of a feeding tube directly into the stomach through the abdominal wall, allowing for enteral nutrition to be administered effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">242881af1a0439ab16c10b788cff01fd,9c43759c41fe226a2702de300b9e580a,e3370b71146ad5063d6b1e9c3d8a3bd2</data>
