      <data key="d6">421</data>
      <data key="d7">195b9196963d4d3f822add6c1274b844</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DOBRATZ">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dobratz is a researcher who evaluated predictive equations for measuring basal metabolic expenditure in obese women.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">422</data>
      <data key="d7">8829a293ad50448dba2425173d7904a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIRUG&#205;A METAB&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Metabolic surgery is a medical procedure recommended for treating type 2 diabetes in patients with obesity.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d3">7</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">423</data>
      <data key="d7">65c68cc0e28244a68dd4cf0a17364f63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL refers to the provision of dietary assistance to patients who are unable to meet their nutritional needs through normal eating. This type of nutritional support is particularly crucial for patients who have undergone metabolic surgery, especially in cases where complications arise. It serves as a necessary intervention to ensure that these patients receive adequate nutrition during their recovery process.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451</data>
      <data key="d3">12</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">424</data>
      <data key="d7">0645281b7a4a4665a46912a0b829b379</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, or parenteral nutrition (NP), is a medical treatment that provides essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. This method is utilized primarily in patients who are unable to consume food orally or tolerate enteral nutrition, particularly in cases such as pancreatitis or post-surgery recovery. During hospitalization, parenteral nutrition serves as an alternative means of nutritional support, ensuring that patients receive adequate nourishment when traditional feeding methods are not viable or contraindicated. Overall, NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is a critical intervention for maintaining the nutritional status of patients who cannot meet their dietary needs through oral or enteral means.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315,3dfc700a2eaec232c05b0a53f2089229,445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce,4b4f297dec86d7f65e362ad688bbb28f,57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009,5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d,88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe</data>
      <data key="d3">21</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">425</data>
      <data key="d7">27037172231e4a5fb397129aa57cbf45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUGA ANASTOM&#211;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fuga anastom&#243;tica is a common complication after metabolic surgery that may require nutritional support due to its impact on oral intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">426</data>
      <data key="d7">0b7d7f06addc47a39ab76a6de150bfe3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NA&#218;SEAS Y V&#211;MITOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nauseas y v&#243;mitos are common post-operative complications that can limit a patient's ability to eat normally after metabolic surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">427</data>
      <data key="d7">fc37c83a37884d47b79eeb8c72c469eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALABSORCI&#211;N SEVERA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Malabsorci&#243;n severa is a serious condition that can occur post-surgery, affecting nutrient absorption and necessitating nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">428</data>
      <data key="d7">0a1a816949da4548813098b393fc555e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA ORAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dieta oral refers to the normal diet that most patients transition to after metabolic surgery, although some may face complications that prevent this.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">429</data>
      <data key="d7">24119a256a0942939a9e1497d6964787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALORIMETR&#205;A INDIRECTA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Calorimetr&#237;a indirecta is a method used to measure basal metabolic rate, which is important for determining nutritional needs in post-operative patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">430</data>
      <data key="d7">54a0cb63cd07458ca2b69d83ee79ffc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EQUACIONES PREDICTIVAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ecuaciones predictivas are formulas used to estimate metabolic expenditure in patients, especially when calorimetry is unavailable.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">431</data>
      <data key="d7">9475efd42f75407cb34f653996024fb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOCIEDAD AMERICANA DE NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ASPEN is an organization that provides guidelines for nutritional support in hospitalized adult obese patients, particularly in the context of bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">432</data>
      <data key="d7">b55a6d0a23144994a8590c7d4e6527b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N HIPERPROTEICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperproteic nutrition is recommended for patients without severe liver or kidney dysfunction, aiming to avoid negative consequences of overfeeding.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d3">14</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">433</data>
      <data key="d7">2026c5df861246d98b06dc51cff81e76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N HIPOCAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypocaloric nutrition is designed to prevent negative outcomes associated with overfeeding, such as hyperglycemia and increased infection rates.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d3">14</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">434</data>
      <data key="d7">aed45c6104ea468996a4c029195aaa3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNIDAD DE CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Intensive Care Unit (UCI) is a specialized department in hospitals where patients receive close monitoring and care, particularly for nutritional adjustments.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d3">14</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">435</data>
      <data key="d7">b170d9ede8cc4985b8259c3b6c4129b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL DE RECOMENDACI&#211;N BAJO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A low level of recommendation indicates that the evidence supporting a particular nutritional approach is not strong, as seen in the guidelines for nutritional support in bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">436</data>
      <data key="d7">a9adf6df87604120abe42f3f198b23c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES DE CUIDADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Levels of care refer to the different intensities of medical care provided, particularly in the context of monitoring nutritional intake in critical patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">437</data>
      <data key="d7">77e4055503aa40e795a744648f293626</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PAR&#193;METROS CL&#205;NICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Clinical parameters are metrics used to assess a patient's health status, including wound healing and early mobilization in the context of nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">438</data>
      <data key="d7">d8d61b116cfa4514bea7eca997f1032b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEFICIENCIAS NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional deficiencies are conditions that arise when the body does not get enough nutrients, which can be a risk for patients undergoing bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">439</data>
      <data key="d7">7b3fe8b1aa514cc1a75216fa44ddc1cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLUIDOS Y ELECTROLITOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fluids and electrolytes are essential for maintaining hydration and electrolyte balance, which must be closely monitored in patients receiving nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">440</data>
      <data key="d7">afa2d93998cf47d484a4f146cdc88e01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES DE GLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Blood glucose levels are monitored to manage the metabolic state of patients, particularly those undergoing bariatric surgery.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">441</data>
      <data key="d7">fc63ddee41e84de6ae5679a3b1945d06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO MORALES MESEGUER">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospital General Universitario Morales Meseguer is a healthcare institution located in Murcia, specializing in various medical fields including endocrinology and nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
