    </node>
    <node id="MURCIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Murcia is a region in Spain where the Hospital General Universitario Morales Meseguer is located.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">444</data>
      <data key="d7">e267bc71626647fb9f6a94710875baae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MNGIE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MNGIE, or mitochondrial neurogastrointestinal encephalomyopathy, is a rare genetic disorder characterized by a deficiency in thymidine phosphorylase, which is caused by mutations in the TYMP gene. This disorder primarily affects the gastrointestinal and nervous systems, resulting in a range of metabolic issues and complications, including diabetes. Due to the complexity of the symptoms and the interplay between the affected systems, MNGIE requires intricate treatment approaches to manage its severe manifestations.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88,763c8ac63b4c91616bcea6f1f4aa38c9,b8db8cc3349b8ac0cce45497da6244fc,cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">35</data>
      <data key="d6">445</data>
      <data key="d7">3f41f3274a774c35bd8bfd7abf06f70e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICIONAL SUPPLEMENTS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional supplements are products taken to enhance dietary intake, often used in clinical settings to support patients with specific health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">446</data>
      <data key="d7">8f9ebbea13c54bb4bd59e841bb9c0db6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FENOFIBRATO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fenofibrate is a medication used to reduce cholesterol levels and triglycerides in the blood, often prescribed for patients with metabolic disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">447</data>
      <data key="d7">9be48f775ec8477eaf58048c06023549</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OMEPRAZOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Omeprazol is a medication that the patient is taking to reduce the production of acid in the stomach. It is commonly used to treat gastroesophageal reflux disease and other related conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88,5cf8b1c5491f78fda9bca97f3d14c5a2</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">448</data>
      <data key="d7">bfd98fd2d1e34292b592fb55bc1d0636</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPLEMENTOS VITAM&#205;NICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vitamin supplements are dietary supplements that provide vitamins, often used to address deficiencies in patients with specific health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">449</data>
      <data key="d7">048c71f7b70f486caee562e55f765e94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BARIATRIC SURGERY">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88</data>
      <data key="d3">20</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">450</data>
      <data key="d7">da21322090ba443ab0a268c9ee3b7289</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROPAT&#205;A &#211;PTICA BILATERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La neuropat&#237;a &#243;ptica bilateral es un diagn&#243;stico que se presenta a los 10-12 a&#241;os, caracterizado por la disminuci&#243;n progresiva de la agudeza visual y la atrofia &#243;ptica observada en el fondo de ojo.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">451</data>
      <data key="d7">be3d77d7e5ea430aa84a663fb60ab12d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLINEUROPAT&#205;A SENSITIVO MOTORA AXONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La polineuropat&#237;a sensitivo motora axonal es un diagn&#243;stico que se presenta a los 16 a&#241;os, caracterizado por debilidad progresiva en miembros y amiotrofia distal.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">452</data>
      <data key="d7">4493e6abcace4b08ba361d0c46b9edfc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOACUSIA PROFUNDA BILATERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hipoacusia profunda bilateral neurosensorial es un diagn&#243;stico que se presenta a los 30 a&#241;os, que requiere la colocaci&#243;n de un implante coclear debido a la severidad de la p&#233;rdida auditiva.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">453</data>
      <data key="d7">008dcd88af7945718f400512943d3af4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEUCOENCEFALOPAT&#205;A SUPRATENTORIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La leucoencefalopat&#237;a supratentorial periventricular difusa es un hallazgo observado en la resonancia magn&#233;tica nuclear cerebral, indicando cambios en la sustancia blanca del cerebro.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">454</data>
      <data key="d7">9b0d9067ef3947adbf0ab75d42c62655</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NTOMAS DIGESTIVOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los s&#237;ntomas digestivos incluyen p&#233;rdida de peso, deposiciones blandas y episodios diarreicos, que se presentan en el paciente a lo largo del tiempo.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">455</data>
      <data key="d7">4fe6f5d09ad9421abdce2163bfd50d68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AN&#193;LISIS DE SANGRE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "AN&#193;LISIS DE SANGRE" refers to blood tests conducted on patients to assess various health indicators. These tests are essential for monitoring glucose levels, renal function, and other critical health parameters. The blood analysis reveals several important metrics, including blood sugar (glucemia), cholesterol levels, and vitamin concentrations, all of which are relevant for diagnosing the patient's health status. Overall, blood tests serve as a vital tool in evaluating the patient's overall health and nutritional parameters.</data>
      <data key="d2">17b7995dcf275c50629c7e3d4723882e,8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">456</data>
      <data key="d7">ba036aaedb074c038632d4a522df0a46</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENDOSCOPIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La endoscopia revela mucosa con atrofia parcheada y linfangiectasias, lo que contribuye al diagn&#243;stico del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">457</data>
      <data key="d7">b042292fb5884cb3b34afe1cda5c232f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;PSULA ENDOSC&#211;PICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La c&#225;psula endosc&#243;pica visualiza linfangiectasias y edema en el yeyuno proximal, proporcionando informaci&#243;n adicional sobre la condici&#243;n del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">458</data>
      <data key="d7">78dd1b612184401d8139e31800925583</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATROFIA &#211;PTICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La atrofia &#243;ptica es un hallazgo observado en el fondo de ojo del paciente, indicando da&#241;o severo en la v&#237;a visual.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">459</data>
      <data key="d7">14276039557e46f1a12161316ab027ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEBILIDAD PROGRESIVA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La debilidad progresiva es un s&#237;ntoma que se presenta a los 16 a&#241;os, afectando principalmente a los miembros inferiores y superiores.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">460</data>
      <data key="d7">7ca2f309686b491aab1041729c12fdb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOGLICEMIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las hipoglucemias son episodios que ocurren debido a la suspensi&#243;n irregular del tratamiento antidiab&#233;tico, afectando la salud del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">461</data>
      <data key="d7">70e2907da8224ef88b8affe8e6bf359d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENSACI&#211;N DE PLENITUD POSTPRANDIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La sensaci&#243;n de plenitud postprandial es un s&#237;ntoma que el paciente experimenta despu&#233;s de las comidas, indicando problemas digestivos.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">462</data>
      <data key="d7">5378126580b847fdb2509d63c56f4961</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IMAGEN DE RMN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La imagen de resonancia magn&#233;tica nuclear (RMN) muestra cambios en la sustancia blanca del cerebro, lo que es relevante para el diagn&#243;stico del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">463</data>
      <data key="d7">4aef504187ad4c9e839d1235f010de57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUCOSA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La mucosa intestinal presenta atrofia y linfangiectasias, lo que se observa durante la endoscopia y es relevante para el diagn&#243;stico del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">464</data>
      <data key="d7">5480750e3edc45e4ba4e429c68943f2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PATOLOG&#205;AS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">465</data>
      <data key="d7">2c8804a259b84a0ea3cef4d4924f74cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TYMP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The TYMP gene is located on chromosome 22q13.33 and encodes a protein involved in the phosphorylation of thymidine, mutations in which cause MNGIE.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">466</data>
      <data key="d7">fc02276ced024066a39e8da7b1ca712d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GARONE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Garone is a researcher who reviewed 102 cases of MNGIE between 1988 and 2011, contributing to the understanding of the syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">467</data>
      <data key="d7">993f19df80264cf98671b585c18572a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIMIDINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Thymidine is a nucleoside that accumulates in patients with MNGIE due to the deficiency of thymidine phosphorylase.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">468</data>
      <data key="d7">a96bfc954ed245b8931401b9ecb8f3f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEOXIURIDINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Deoxyuridine is another nucleoside that accumulates in patients with MNGIE, indicating a metabolic disturbance.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">469</data>
      <data key="d7">092ba38abc6f491a9677545237e64dba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALHAMIA PRISON">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Alhamia Prison is a facility mentioned in the context of MNGIE, although not directly related to the syndrome itself.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">470</data>
