    <node id="PANCREATITIS AGUDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acute pancreatitis is a medical condition characterized by inflammation of the pancreas, which can lead to tissue damage and affect other organs. This condition often manifests with symptoms that arise between 24 and 36 hours following the peak production of cytokines. In the case of the patient, acute pancreatitis was experienced prior to the diagnosis of a tumor, necessitating intensive treatment and monitoring. Additionally, careful nutritional management is crucial for patients with acute pancreatitis, particularly for those who are diabetic.</data>
      <data key="d2">57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009,5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d,7c10030e29c1434df3b10b1533710486,88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e,a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944</data>
      <data key="d3">21</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">24</data>
      <data key="d6">507</data>
      <data key="d7">9b384fcca57649f28da832f6b2cf91c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UCI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Unidad de Cuidados Intensivos (UCI), also known as the Intensive Care Unit, is a specialized area within a hospital dedicated to providing critical care to patients facing severe health challenges. This unit is particularly equipped to manage patients with serious conditions, such as severe pancreatitis, and is designed to handle complications that may arise during treatment. Patients requiring intensive monitoring and advanced medical interventions are transferred to the UCI to ensure they receive the highest level of care during critical situations.</data>
      <data key="d2">5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d,a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944</data>
      <data key="d3">21</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">508</data>
      <data key="d7">173443a0eec14fd3a36352cba6ceb9a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DUODENOPANCREATECTOM&#205;A SUBTOTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Subtotal duodenopancreatectomy is the surgical procedure performed on the patient to address the pancreatic tumor.</data>
      <data key="d2">a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944</data>
      <data key="d3">21</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">509</data>
      <data key="d7">22ed9b9379c04a9295b237da106745e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TAC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TAC, or Tomograf&#237;a Axial Computarizada, is a medical imaging technique utilized to monitor a patient's condition over time, particularly for the detection of lesions. In this case, a CT scan was performed, revealing irregularities in the pancreatic process along with other findings. The procedure specifically aimed to confirm the dilation of the Wirsung duct in the patient, highlighting its importance in diagnosing and assessing pancreatic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944,b00c312f46e790b32fe99743480f9e47,cba5d81f1acff7cbf84e85ef35420521</data>
      <data key="d3">9</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">510</data>
      <data key="d7">1e6ce0b317124f9e81b1b08c4fa56409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RMN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Magnetic Resonance Imaging (RMN) was conducted to suggest the presence of a mucinous tumor in the patient.</data>
      <data key="d2">a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">511</data>
      <data key="d7">4d0a5619b3234ba58ea2353912ed266a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIOPSIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A biopsy was performed via endoscopic ultrasound to confirm the diagnosis of the pancreatic mucinous tumor.</data>
      <data key="d2">a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944</data>
      <data key="d3">21</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">512</data>
      <data key="d7">0c0af9ef53584a0ab8afdd4bc1e7b097</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMODI&#193;LISIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemodialysis was required by the patient due to renal failure during their stay in the UCI.</data>
      <data key="d2">a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944</data>
      <data key="d3">21</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">513</data>
      <data key="d7">9e25055e7fd246b3a92b899153bf684b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SANGRADO MASIVO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Massive bleeding occurred post-surgery, necessitating urgent intervention for the patient.</data>
      <data key="d2">a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944</data>
      <data key="d3">21</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">514</data>
      <data key="d7">90175f45748540e889f94751dcb2a5da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEHISCENCIA DE LA ANASTOMOSIS PANCREATOYEYUNAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dehiscence of the pancreatojejunostomy occurred, leading to further complications for the patient.</data>
      <data key="d2">a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944</data>
      <data key="d3">21</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">515</data>
      <data key="d7">aef7fa2be3d64dd583a12852d9bf532e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PANCREATITIS AGUDA NECR&#211;TICO HEMORR&#193;GICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acute necrotizing hemorrhagic pancreatitis developed in the patient, complicating their recovery.</data>
      <data key="d2">a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944</data>
      <data key="d3">21</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">516</data>
      <data key="d7">e3f2ec7298d143db98c48116c279d02d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPLICACIONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">COMPLICACIONES refer to the various health issues that arise as a result of a patient's diabetes. During hospitalization, the patient experienced multiple complications related to their condition and treatment, highlighting the significant impact that diabetes can have on overall health and the potential challenges faced in managing the disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944,acd36e6dbcd98757c4cf33ff090764ee</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">517</data>
      <data key="d7">cfc942fe75e64e6983f30439d29a929e</data>
    </node>
