    </node>
    <node id="SPANISH SOCIETY OF ENDOCRINOLOGY AND NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition (SEEN) is an organization focused on the study and management of endocrine and nutritional issues, including diabetes and metabolic control.</data>
      <data key="d2">e36c9b09870e14d19aa6eb7c82514499</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">536</data>
      <data key="d7">7b5ce8ef1b8f4e958768b2d03f2945cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="A.S.P.E.N.">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (A.S.P.E.N.) provides clinical guidelines for nutrition support in patients, particularly those with hyperglycemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">e36c9b09870e14d19aa6eb7c82514499</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">537</data>
      <data key="d7">768f5422be8f4af3ae42b267acb4ccaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GARIN GROUP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The GARIN group is the Andalusian Group for Nutrition Reflection and Investigation, which focuses on managing patients with diabetes and stress hyperglycemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">e36c9b09870e14d19aa6eb7c82514499</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">538</data>
      <data key="d7">b621e1190a2d4308aa24db7dfda99702</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERGLYCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperglycemia is a medical condition characterized by an excessive amount of glucose in the blood. It is often seen in patients with diabetes and may require dietary intervention to manage blood sugar levels effectively. If left untreated, hyperglycemia can lead to severe complications, highlighting the importance of monitoring and controlling blood sugar levels in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">178140d0d29364593546d7d21393f2c6,acd36e6dbcd98757c4cf33ff090764ee,e36c9b09870e14d19aa6eb7c82514499</data>
      <data key="d3">4</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">539</data>
      <data key="d7">4755e198f39747358db749c5aa6d9c4f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PANCREATICODUODENECTOMY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pancreaticoduodenectomy is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of the pancreas and duodenum, often requiring specialized nutritional support post-surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">e36c9b09870e14d19aa6eb7c82514499</data>
      <data key="d3">4</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">540</data>
      <data key="d7">b590a18069604a41bf920022e48e706d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITION SUPPORT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrition support refers to the provision of nutrients and nutritional therapy to patients who are unable to eat or absorb sufficient nutrients due to various medical conditions, such as acute pancreatitis. This support is essential for individuals who cannot meet their nutritional needs through normal eating, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients for recovery and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,e36c9b09870e14d19aa6eb7c82514499</data>
      <data key="d3">4</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">541</data>
      <data key="d7">31b811f6dfcb4890b3f80da355b4a981</data>
    </node>
