    <node id="ANA ISABEL S&#193;NCHEZ MARCOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dra. Ana Isabel S&#225;nchez Marcos is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, focusing on eating disorders in patients with diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">7949b821c1ca2e4adc524e7775626396</data>
      <data key="d3">5</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">581</data>
      <data key="d7">cc3b1f30dcc741f9bfe553d55a354d8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNO DEL COMPORTAMIENTO ALIMENTARIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"TRASTORNO DEL COMPORTAMIENTO ALIMENTARIO," or Eating Disorders (TCA), refers to a group of psychiatric diseases that are marked by significant medical complications. These disorders are characterized by persistent disturbances in food intake, which can impair both health and psychosocial functioning. Additionally, this condition notably affects patients with diabetes, particularly young women diagnosed with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus (DM1).</data>
      <data key="d2">7949b821c1ca2e4adc524e7775626396,bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">5</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">582</data>
      <data key="d7">c735ab7293344eb3ab7c57d182c7c590</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 (DM1) is a chronic condition that has been managed by the patient for 6 years, characterized by poor glycemic control. This condition occurs when the pancreas produces little or no insulin, necessitating continuous management of insulin and blood glucose levels. Additionally, Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 poses a higher risk for developing eating disorders, particularly in young women, which can complicate the careful management required for the condition. Overall, DM1 demands vigilant monitoring and a comprehensive approach to treatment to maintain health and mitigate associated risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec,48f1fe343d54cd0f353be34b736a352c,7949b821c1ca2e4adc524e7775626396,a960ccbf15a28151d1461c4203408408</data>
      <data key="d3">5</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">583</data>
      <data key="d7">1679d4b255fe425098c53ed292e26089</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERCALORIC DIABETES-SPECIFIC ENTERAL NUTRITIONAL FORMULA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A specialized nutritional formula designed for patients with diabetes to improve their nutritional status and glycemic control.</data>
      <data key="d2">7949b821c1ca2e4adc524e7775626396</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">584</data>
      <data key="d7">c20b08c6fa964a26a585bf19a1c945d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES TECHNOLOGY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes technology refers to the tools and methods used to manage diabetes, including enteral formulas and monitoring devices.</data>
      <data key="d2">7949b821c1ca2e4adc524e7775626396</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">585</data>
      <data key="d7">7bcc6ed069b34f629ff04d853802a516</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES MELLITUS TYPE 1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 (DM1) is an autoimmune disease characterized by chronic insulin deficiency. This condition necessitates careful management of diet and physical activity to effectively control blood sugar levels. It is a chronic condition that can lead to various complications, and in this particular case, it was diagnosed in the patient at the age of 28.</data>
      <data key="d2">acd36e6dbcd98757c4cf33ff090764ee,bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">5</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">586</data>
      <data key="d7">47f6c4241af9468d93a0df8288d761f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMERICAN PSYCHIATRIC ASSOCIATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Psychiatric Association is a professional organization that publishes the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM-5), which includes criteria for diagnosing eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">5</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">587</data>
      <data key="d7">d3e8935752be4c3cb7438dbae698329d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUNDACI&#211;N SED">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Fundaci&#243;n SED is an organization in Spain that provides data and support for individuals with diabetes, including statistics on the prevalence of diabetes in minors.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">5</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">588</data>
      <data key="d7">76ebcb4ca2cd46d09aaa0b6eece40419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anorexia Nervosa is an eating disorder marked by an intense fear of gaining weight and a distorted body image, leading to severe food restriction and health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">5</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">589</data>
      <data key="d7">381a32f5346d495eaa24bf72e71796ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNO DE EVITACI&#211;N/RESTRICCI&#211;N DE ALIMENTOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Avoidant/Restrictive Food Intake Disorder is characterized by a lack of interest in eating or avoidance of certain foods, which can lead to nutritional deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">5</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">590</data>
      <data key="d7">c5ccc70c93cb4351ad914c5dc9263a04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNO DE ATRACONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Binge Eating Disorder involves recurrent episodes of eating large quantities of food, often to the point of discomfort, and is associated with feelings of loss of control.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">5</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">591</data>
