    <node id="TCA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TCA, or Trastorno de la Conducta Alimentaria, refers to an eating disorder that the patient is struggling with, characterized by restrictive eating and purging behaviors. This disorder is particularly prevalent among patients with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus (DM1), especially young women, and it can exacerbate the complications associated with diabetes. The specific manifestations of TCA in this context include food restriction and the omission of insulin, which can significantly impact the patient's health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f685a05a9682db6dcde958d1918cc77,410fab643c125e0f8944ebae5dba5ec0,48f1fe343d54cd0f353be34b736a352c</data>
      <data key="d3">5</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
