    <node id="UTCA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">UTCA, or Unidad de Trastornos de la Conducta Alimentaria, is a specialized healthcare facility dedicated to the treatment of eating disorders. It offers comprehensive care that addresses both nutritional and psychological issues faced by patients. The unit operates through a collaborative approach, integrating the expertise of various disciplines, including Psychiatry, Psychology, and Endocrinology, to provide holistic treatment tailored to the needs of individuals struggling with these disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec,933d6526b2d313c95c9f4aaa950a62a3</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">606</data>
      <data key="d7">84fa2282b6214ac48b6949a5bde5bb4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANAMNESIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anamnesis is a detailed assessment process that includes the patient's medical history, dietary habits, and psychological factors related to eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">607</data>
      <data key="d7">739c7b6f587d40dabc61fe413efddec0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALORACI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "VALORACI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL" refers to the process of assessing a patient's nutritional status and needs. This comprehensive evaluation includes the use of clinical and anthropometric markers to determine the individual's nutritional state. At UTCA, the nutritional assessment encompasses various tests and evaluations aimed at understanding the patient's eating habits and overall nutritional status. Through these methods, "VALORACI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL" provides a thorough understanding of a patient's dietary requirements and health.</data>
      <data key="d2">1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec,5549895a3a7f54651e6c54f5a5d7d833,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5</data>
      <data key="d3">11</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">608</data>
      <data key="d7">d53a3028d49c4390a23b1271d3c481d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTROPOMETR&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ANTROPOMETR&#205;A refers to the practice of measuring the human body's physical dimensions and body composition. This field is essential for assessing an individual's health and nutritional status. By evaluating these measurements, healthcare professionals can gain insights into a person's physical health and overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">609</data>
      <data key="d7">01c81b9a1739491eb03495f87635f1a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ECG">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Electrocardiogram (ECG) is a test performed to monitor the patient's heart activity and detect any abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d2">1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">610</data>
      <data key="d7">c9ecf89468a649ca93195a73bf13abaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANAL&#205;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ANAL&#205;TICA refers to the laboratory tests conducted to evaluate a patient's biochemical markers and overall health status. These analytical tests are essential for monitoring various blood parameters, including blood counts, enzyme levels, blood sugar levels, and nutritional deficiencies. By assessing these factors, ANAL&#205;TICA provides valuable insights into the patient's condition, helping healthcare professionals make informed decisions regarding diagnosis and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec,319591d16b552cff77a5cd56e69c1ca2,933d6526b2d313c95c9f4aaa950a62a3,b00c312f46e790b32fe99743480f9e47</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
