    <node id="HBA1C">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">HbA1c is a blood test that measures average blood glucose levels over the past 2 to 3 months, making it an essential tool for managing diabetes. It indicates the patient's glycemic control, with values consistently above 8.5% suggesting poor management of blood sugar levels. Throughout treatment, HbA1c levels are monitored to assess the effectiveness of diabetes management strategies. In a recent analysis, the patient's HbA1c result was recorded at 6.2%, indicating good control of her diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec,3f685a05a9682db6dcde958d1918cc77,5cf8b1c5491f78fda9bca97f3d14c5a2,6edff59a3b151e946e7664f13bcb0931,bfdbf41efa08067d5ae1b1a67830affd,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b</data>
