    <node id="P&#201;RDIDA DE PESO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"P&#201;RDIDA DE PESO" refers to a significant health condition observed in patients, characterized by a notable reduction in body weight. In this specific case, the patient experienced a weight loss of 5 kg over the six months leading up to their referral, with a more substantial overall weight loss amounting to 10 kg during their hospital stay. The percentage of weight loss in this context ranges from 13% to 17%, highlighting the severity of the condition. Weight loss is a common occurrence among cancer patients, often linked to the disease itself and the effects of its treatments. This condition is a critical factor in medical assessments, as it can indicate the progression of the illness and the patient's overall health status.</data>
      <data key="d2">3356667d6f35de6a8587ece00f8c6580,4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a,514518b96e32b025815b45cc2a504f0d,83b82871866963bb43f901dd9ca09fcb,e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5</data>
