    <node id="MECV-V">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MECV-V is a clinical evaluation method designed for the assessment of swallowing difficulties, particularly in patients who have experienced a stroke. It serves as a tool for monitoring dysphagia, which refers to difficulties in swallowing. The MECV-V test specifically focuses on volume viscosity, aiding in the diagnosis of swallowing challenges. This method evaluates both the safety and efficiency of swallowing, providing crucial insights into the patient's condition and guiding further treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a,7469cc60475806b519e91abe2796aead,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451</data>
      <data key="d3">22</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">841</data>
      <data key="d7">c82c3a8019a04809a233f34c889b1ee0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITION ENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrition enteral (NE) is a method of delivering nutrition directly to the stomach or intestine through a tube. This approach is specifically utilized for patients who may have difficulty consuming food orally, such as those recovering from surgery. By providing nutrition directly into the gastrointestinal tract, enteral nutrition ensures that patients receive the necessary nutrients for healing and recovery.</data>
      <data key="d2">7a6970183393c5ef1adc99851ef3eada,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451</data>
      <data key="d3">22</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">842</data>
      <data key="d7">186e070274ac47368d15d43a641b3147</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DESNUTRICI&#211;N MODERADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"DESNUTRICI&#211;N MODERADA" refers to a condition diagnosed in the patient, characterized by a significant deficiency in nutritional intake. The diagnosis is based on the GLIM criteria, which indicate a notable loss of weight and essential nutrients. This condition necessitated the implementation of a nutritional treatment plan to address the patient's health and recovery needs. Overall, moderate malnutrition signifies that the patient is experiencing insufficient nutritional intake, which adversely affects their overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">82d36ebbaaa026c713df2b7a47253efa,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451,c92ceeeeae88c8288176cbfd00c75e17,ce4c057e0a625bc9e64301a0cca1e206</data>
