    <node id="GASTROSTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrostom&#237;a is a surgical procedure that involves creating an opening in the stomach through the abdominal wall, allowing for the placement of a tube that facilitates enteral feeding. This procedure is particularly beneficial for patients who require nutritional support, such as those with low weight or difficulties in oral feeding. The patient in question underwent this procedure at the age of 15 to address their feeding needs and is currently utilizing the gastrostomy tube for nocturnal nutrition. Overall, gastrostom&#237;a serves as an essential medical intervention for individuals requiring long-term feeding support.</data>
      <data key="d2">7469cc60475806b519e91abe2796aead,84e91b50850bfa0ad0122cdebf477a1d,bfdbf41efa08067d5ae1b1a67830affd,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b,e7df0ed14559db764d393fb9411fec33</data>
