    <node id="DIABETES RELACIONADA CON LA FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes related to cystic fibrosis (DRFQ) is a significant health condition that affects individuals with cystic fibrosis. It is recognized as the most common non-respiratory complication in cystic fibrosis patients, with a prevalence of approximately 20%. One patient has been managing this diabetes condition since the age of 14, necessitating insulin treatment to help control their blood sugar levels. However, this patient has experienced poor glycemic control, highlighting the challenges associated with managing diabetes in the context of cystic fibrosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b</data>
