    <node id="DRFQ">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DRFQ refers to a specific type of diabetes diagnosed in patients, necessitating management and treatment strategies that include insulin administration and nutritional education. Additionally, it is associated with malnutrition related to cystic fibrosis, a condition that can worsen the prognosis of patients suffering from this genetic disorder. This highlights the importance of comprehensive care in managing both diabetes and the nutritional challenges faced by individuals with cystic fibrosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f295222427803a7fc92b83386e5ec56,dc7539b4d637d6dd09963c2564f4f084</data>
