      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">974</data>
      <data key="d7">510a5c9b4d914f559c3d180ca4d19370</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AFAGIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Afagia es la incapacidad para tragar, que puede ser consecuencia de intervenciones quir&#250;rgicas o condiciones m&#233;dicas.</data>
      <data key="d2">e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">975</data>
      <data key="d7">fb5461f067ac4400becab6582d94ef7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUCOSITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mucositis is the inflammation of the mucous membranes, often occurring as a side effect of radiotherapy. It is a common complication in patients undergoing radiotherapy and chemotherapy, significantly impacting their ability to eat.</data>
      <data key="d2">5aa4da1a8d1e0b60ec7e801c7db1701c,e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">976</data>
      <data key="d7">f494f828e23d4318aa59a3ce1611a0f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPLEMENTOS NUTRICIONALES ORALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Suplementos nutricionales orales son productos dise&#241;ados para complementar la dieta y proporcionar nutrientes adicionales, utilizados en pacientes con deficiencias nutricionales.</data>
      <data key="d2">e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d3">21</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">977</data>
      <data key="d7">9f000bcdf8754d53845d0172e737723c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNIDAD DE NUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La Unidad de Nutrici&#243;n es un departamento m&#233;dico que se encarga de evaluar y ajustar la nutrici&#243;n de los pacientes, especialmente aquellos con condiciones complejas como c&#225;ncer.</data>
      <data key="d2">e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">978</data>
      <data key="d7">bd6b84a928624dd3b36abbbebe799aa2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CCEE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">CCEE, or Consultas Externas Especializadas, refers to specialized medical services that provide care to patients who do not require continuous hospitalization. These services focus on offering specialized follow-up and treatment, ensuring that patients receive the necessary medical attention without the need for an inpatient stay.</data>
      <data key="d2">4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a,49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40,e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">979</data>
      <data key="d7">f3392b027b7d486aaca0ea64a6e16122</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RIESGO NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Riesgo nutricional se refiere a la posibilidad de que un paciente no reciba suficientes nutrientes, especialmente en el contexto de enfermedades como el c&#225;ncer.</data>
      <data key="d2">e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">980</data>
      <data key="d7">e7a10fbdeff446c89f509fde08c0c9fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTERVENCI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Intervenci&#243;n nutricional es el proceso de evaluar y modificar la dieta de un paciente para mejorar su estado nutricional, especialmente en pacientes oncol&#243;gicos.</data>
      <data key="d2">e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">981</data>
      <data key="d7">6fc7dd56759e417ab1831642265af650</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUIMIOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">QUIMIOTERAPIA, or chemotherapy, is a treatment method primarily used for cancer that involves the administration of drugs designed to kill cancer cells. This approach is often employed in the management of various types of cancer, including pancreatic cancer. While chemotherapy can be an effective option, particularly after surgical interventions, it is associated with several complications and side effects. Patients undergoing chemotherapy may experience issues such as hyperglycemia and cachexia, which can significantly impact their nutritional status. Overall, chemotherapy is a critical component in cancer treatment, but it requires careful management due to its potential adverse effects on the patient's health and nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,a960ccbf15a28151d1461c4203408408,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3,da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc,e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">982</data>
      <data key="d7">6cf8a143bb874044a88816e0cfe6cce9</data>
    </node>
