      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">984</data>
      <data key="d7">7807077b4a3a4e3e80146ab1a94c7c47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ORL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ORL refers to the Otorrinolaringolog&#237;a department, also known as the field of Otolaryngology, which specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of conditions related to the ear, nose, and throat. In this context, ORL is where the patient was referred for evaluation and treatment of laryngeal carcinoma. The department is actively involved in the patient's treatment and follow-up care, ensuring comprehensive management of their condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a,49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">985</data>
      <data key="d7">f8391b5d490a40c5b2ad9a3b15a6f0c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GRP refers to a prophylactic gastrostomy placement that was requested for the patient, serving as a medical intervention to provide nutritional support. This type of feeding tube is utilized for patients who are unable to take food orally, indicating its importance in ensuring adequate nutrition. The gastrostomy route through which the patient received this nutritional support is critical for their recovery post-surgery, highlighting the essential role of GRP in the patient's overall treatment plan.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a,49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40,5aa4da1a8d1e0b60ec7e801c7db1701c</data>
      <data key="d3">19</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">986</data>
      <data key="d7">b419b6a43424438085afbc16c7f3c0a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALNUTRITION SCREENING TOOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Malnutrition Screening Tool (MST) is a standardized instrument designed to evaluate the risk of malnutrition in patients. It is utilized in clinical settings to identify individuals who may be at risk, allowing for timely intervention and management of their nutritional needs. The MST was specifically applied to this patient to assess their malnutrition risk.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,7a6970183393c5ef1adc99851ef3eada</data>
      <data key="d3">22</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">987</data>
      <data key="d7">a8ca70505b9c412eb087d45268021d57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VAR&#211;N DE 66 A&#209;OS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The patient is a 66-year-old male who has undergone surgery for laryngeal carcinoma and is receiving nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">988</data>
      <data key="d7">4165c7e2f002417d8c6d1dec257c4cdd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOMOGRAF&#205;A COMPUTERIZADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tomograf&#237;a computerizada (CT) is a diagnostic imaging procedure that revealed the extent of the patient's cancer.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">989</data>
      <data key="d7">a28c74f33d7f4855837e7433c1ad24ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AC&#218;FENOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ac&#250;fenos refers to the ringing or buzzing in the ears that the patient experienced, prompting further medical evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">990</data>
      <data key="d7">514e1ff20205422096c682be8f1e0283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOMOGRAF&#205;A COMPUTERIZADA DE CUELLO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tomograf&#237;a computerizada de cuello is a diagnostic imaging procedure that revealed the presence of neoplasia and adenopathies in the patient.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">991</data>
      <data key="d7">86066b75394f4a20a1460cf4f4e96221</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEOPLASIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neoplasia refers to the abnormal growth of tissue, which was identified in the patient's larynx during a CT scan. This condition is characterized by the presence of a tumor, which is pertinent to the patient's medical situation and has implications for their nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">992</data>
      <data key="d7">4ff3711426d848b6aedc36952b435fb0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMIT&#201; DE TUMORES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Comit&#233; de Tumores is a medical committee dedicated to evaluating patients' cases to determine appropriate treatment options for cancer. This committee plays a crucial role in assessing cancer diagnoses and formulating treatment plans, ensuring that patients receive tailored and effective care based on their specific medical needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,3356667d6f35de6a8587ece00f8c6580</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">993</data>
      <data key="d7">d66e586973434f4e96141f139fbd519a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOGLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipo glucemia, also known as hypoglycemia, refers to a condition characterized by abnormally low blood sugar levels. This condition poses a risk to patients, particularly those managing diabetes, especially if they are undergoing insulin therapy. It is crucial for individuals with diabetes to monitor their blood sugar levels closely to prevent the occurrence of hypoglycemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">994</data>
      <data key="d7">eaf741fa4cdd49289ba20b0d2041268e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CENTRO DE ESPECIALIDADES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
