    </node>
    <node id="CANCER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cancer is a disease characterized by uncontrolled cell growth, which can lead to various health complications, including malnutrition and diabetes. It involves the proliferation of abnormal cells, and one specific type of cancer mentioned is pancreatic adenocarcinoma, which is a form of cancer that affects the pancreas.</data>
      <data key="d2">5f4610a3d5efde69d7f34ec14c4bed0b,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">1203</data>
      <data key="d7">a59b812b5e8e4d5f94bbc7140b5c09bc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PANCREATIC CANCER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pancreatic cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the pancreas and is recognized for its aggressive nature and poor prognosis. It is often associated with cachexia, a syndrome that results in significant weight loss and muscle wasting. This form of cancer is characterized by a high mortality rate, making it one of the more challenging cancers to treat effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3,daed781ebc502b854582efdef23e9dde</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">1204</data>
      <data key="d7">9388d907768e471e9808fc6842246ab2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAQUEXIA CANCEROSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cancer cachexia is a syndrome characterized by severe body weight, muscle mass, and fat loss, often seen in patients with advanced cancer.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3</data>
      <data key="d3">10</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1205</data>
      <data key="d7">8dd54c98619941b782bf9340c2031470</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENOCARCINOMA DE P&#193;NCREAS DUCTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adenocarcinoma de p&#225;ncreas ductal is a type of cancer that is frequently associated with cachexia, affecting 70-80% of patients and linked to decreased survival and quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d2">da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">1206</data>
      <data key="d7">e51debed7d4a402284aa82e00904a0bd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NE NORMOCAL&#211;RICA Y NORMOPROTEICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Normocaloric and normoproteic nutritional support with soluble fiber was administered to the patient to normalize weight and regulate intestinal rhythm.</data>
      <data key="d2">da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1207</data>
      <data key="d7">989e38c257994c4c99bc15c2417fd57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes Mellitus (DM) is a condition that worsened the patient's metabolic control, leading to elevated blood glucose levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">1208</data>
      <data key="d7">cb0de727f2ef42e4858b91721ff62f4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEXAMETASONA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dexamethasone is a corticosteroid that is commonly administered during chemotherapy. It has been shown to improve the general condition of patients and contribute to the pharmacological management of hyperglycemia. Additionally, dexamethasone enhances the quality of life and alleviates asthenia in cancer patients, making it a valuable treatment option in oncology settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">5f4610a3d5efde69d7f34ec14c4bed0b,da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">1209</data>
      <data key="d7">f094d5903708409e81a2d973b86e121e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACETATO DE MEDROXIPROGESTERONA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ACETATO DE MEDROXIPROGESTERONA, also known as medroxyprogesterone acetate, is a medication that serves multiple therapeutic purposes. It is primarily recognized for its ability to improve appetite and reduce weight loss, particularly in patients suffering from conditions such as cancer. Additionally, this medication may antagonize the catabolic effects of cytokines, which are often elevated in such patients, thereby helping to mitigate the adverse effects associated with these inflammatory markers. Overall, ACETATO DE MEDROXIPROGESTERONA plays a significant role in enhancing the quality of life for individuals experiencing appetite loss and weight reduction due to various medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">5f4610a3d5efde69d7f34ec14c4bed0b,da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">1210</data>
      <data key="d7">56a071cb01d04191ac255580aad937d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SNO INMUNOMODULADORA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Immunomodulatory nutritional support was not chosen for the patient, focusing instead on specific nutritional support for diabetes management.</data>
      <data key="d2">da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1211</data>
      <data key="d7">c7d8b64383be4fd7891560e9f1afedc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SNO ESPEC&#205;FICA DE DM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Specific nutritional support for diabetes management was recommended, which does not contain omega-3 or nucleotides.</data>
      <data key="d2">da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1212</data>
