    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="DIABETES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The patient has both cystic fibrosis and diabetes, which are interrelated conditions affecting his health</data>
      <data key="d10">84e91b50850bfa0ad0122cdebf477a1d</data>
      <data key="d11">05f4c467013e4f0f8535dbedaec31bc2</data>
      <data key="d12">94</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="F508DEL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The patient has been diagnosed with cystic fibrosis due to the F508del mutation</data>
      <data key="d10">84e91b50850bfa0ad0122cdebf477a1d</data>
      <data key="d11">3f5f825e90fc43a683ca9dcf1482e1bd</data>
      <data key="d12">95</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="PACIENTE">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The patient has been diagnosed with cystic fibrosis, a condition that significantly impacts their overall health and necessitates specific nutritional management. This diagnosis requires careful attention to the patient's nutritional needs to support their health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">3f295222427803a7fc92b83386e5ec56,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b</data>
      <data key="d11">0d1b7840b5ac442fa9272b62ca629618</data>
      <data key="d12">96</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="CFTR">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cystic fibrosis is caused by mutations in the CFTR gene, which is crucial for the disease's pathology.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d11">74966e6e48f645679cd6108bf1686c67</data>
      <data key="d12">97</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="DIABETES RELACIONADA CON LA FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes related to cystic fibrosis is a common complication arising from the disease.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d11">3f60cbffdcbb4035bdd7b645720b6116</data>
      <data key="d12">98</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE&#193;TICA EXOCRINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Exocrine pancreatic insufficiency is a complication of cystic fibrosis that affects the pancreas.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d11">f4188668076d41678991d2c70f822510</data>
      <data key="d12">99</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE&#193;TICA ENDOCRINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Endocrine pancreatic insufficiency is another complication of cystic fibrosis that can lead to diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d11">48a6846d436f4ae5bc5aac8edc14da91</data>
      <data key="d12">100</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="DESNUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Malnutrition is a common complication in cystic fibrosis patients due to malabsorption of nutrients.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d11">8b721b05b544403991589cfd6668e11f</data>
      <data key="d12">101</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="EUROPA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cystic fibrosis has a specific incidence and prevalence in Europe, highlighting its impact in the region.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d11">a140bc26cba64ecfbe4a669d940b8aa3</data>
      <data key="d12">102</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="MUTACI&#211;N F508DEL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The F508del mutation is the most frequent mutation associated with cystic fibrosis, affecting its clinical expression.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d11">b8743dd6cb3c4c54bd6c179dba64efc0</data>
      <data key="d12">103</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="DRFQ">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Desnutrici&#243;n relacionada con la fibrosis qu&#237;stica is a complication that affects the prognosis of patients with cystic fibrosis.</data>
      <data key="d10">3f295222427803a7fc92b83386e5ec56</data>
      <data key="d11">a1fcf0e10eb040c3add16864e575a243</data>
      <data key="d12">104</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL" target="MNGIE">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal must be differentiated from MNGIE</data>
      <data key="d10">b8db8cc3349b8ac0cce45497da6244fc</data>
      <data key="d11">41c40fdd199045a4bc3d26d2b82033ab</data>
      <data key="d12">105</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE P&#193;NCREAS" target="DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 1">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#225;ncer de p&#225;ncreas can complicate the management of Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 due to its impact on health</data>
      <data key="d10">a960ccbf15a28151d1461c4203408408</data>
      <data key="d11">aa6f6355eb114565bdb9d712350c4c59</data>
      <data key="d12">106</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE P&#193;NCREAS" target="ADENOCARCINOMA PANCREATICO DUCTAL">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#225;ncer de p&#225;ncreas is often diagnosed as adenocarcinoma pancre&#225;tico ductal, which is a specific type of pancreatic cancer</data>
      <data key="d10">a960ccbf15a28151d1461c4203408408</data>
      <data key="d11">eba1f997530945b7a161e3ed36353ddb</data>
      <data key="d12">107</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE P&#193;NCREAS" target="S&#205;NDROME PARANEOPL&#193;SICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#225;ncer de p&#225;ncreas can lead to the development of s&#237;ndrome paraneopl&#225;sico in affected patients</data>
      <data key="d10">a960ccbf15a28151d1461c4203408408</data>
      <data key="d11">f1a2cf02f03549988829855a39e8823b</data>
      <data key="d12">108</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE P&#193;NCREAS" target="QUIMIOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Quimioterapia is a common treatment for patients diagnosed with c&#225;ncer de p&#225;ncreas</data>
      <data key="d10">a960ccbf15a28151d1461c4203408408</data>
      <data key="d11">d8c2da25fea64e94855cbe343dbb63cb</data>
      <data key="d12">109</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE P&#193;NCREAS" target="ANEMIA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Anemia can be a complication in patients suffering from c&#225;ncer de p&#225;ncreas due to the disease and its treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">a960ccbf15a28151d1461c4203408408</data>
      <data key="d11">41110cc1d2354aeab8c5b3b24a107d28</data>
      <data key="d12">110</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE P&#193;NCREAS" target="CA 19.9">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CA 19.9 is a tumor marker that is often elevated in patients with c&#225;ncer de p&#225;ncreas</data>
      <data key="d10">a960ccbf15a28151d1461c4203408408</data>
      <data key="d11">c4a4752610204da39d997aced4b878d9</data>
      <data key="d12">111</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="DIABETES MELLITUS">
      <data key="d8">22.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL and DIABETES MELLITUS are closely related in the context of managing nutritional needs in patients with diabetes. Diabetes Mellitus can impact the effectiveness of enteral nutrition, particularly in patients suffering from acute pancreatitis. However, it often necessitates the use of enteral nutrition to effectively manage the dietary requirements of patients, especially those who are hospitalized or elderly. Additionally, enteral nutrition plays a crucial role in addressing the nutritional needs of patients with diabetes mellitus who are experiencing severe malnutrition due to conditions such as MELAS. Overall, enteral nutrition serves as an essential intervention for managing the dietary and nutritional challenges faced by individuals with diabetes mellitus.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ba0aa1d1330351a62eb6319ffdd30db,57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009,8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d11">fefaf32531fb484a9b47e3357c2bc9d6</data>
      <data key="d12">112</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="OLVEIRA ET AL.">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Olveira et al. studied the prevalence of enteral nutrition in hospitalized patients, particularly those with diabetes</data>
      <data key="d10">1ba0aa1d1330351a62eb6319ffdd30db</data>
      <data key="d11">6becc2859e884e69a415e3c9676a5d59</data>
      <data key="d12">113</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="HOSPITAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hospitals often provide enteral nutrition to patients who cannot eat by mouth, including those with diabetes</data>
      <data key="d10">1ba0aa1d1330351a62eb6319ffdd30db</data>
      <data key="d11">89624f45d21a485289bab68cae802ae3</data>
      <data key="d12">114</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="GERIATRIC RESIDENCE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Geriatric residences implement enteral nutrition protocols for elderly patients who require nutritional support</data>
      <data key="d10">1ba0aa1d1330351a62eb6319ffdd30db</data>
      <data key="d11">0a3f5de7834241c7920f928d3e551eb5</data>
      <data key="d12">115</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="S&#205;NDROME DE MELAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enteral nutrition is critical for patients with MELAS to improve their nutritional status and manage complications like diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d10">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d11">4120ad30af16485a8c9bf31179cdcb9d</data>
      <data key="d12">116</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="PACIENTE">
      <data key="d8">60.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The patient has been subjected to enteral nutrition to enhance their nutritional status due to moderate malnutrition. This intervention was deemed necessary because the patient's oral intake was ineffective in meeting their nutritional requirements. Consequently, it was decided to initiate enteral nutrition via a percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy (PEG) due to the patient's inability to fulfill nutritional needs through oral means. Additionally, the patient is receiving enteral nutrition as part of their treatment plan for cystic fibrosis, which further underscores the importance of this nutritional approach. The patient has also received enteral nutrition through a nasogastric tube as part of her treatment. However, there was a point when the patient was not receiving enteral nutrition but had been advised on dietary enrichment, indicating a transition in their nutritional management strategy. Overall, the patient's enteral nutrition is a critical component of their care, aimed at addressing their specific dietary needs effectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">3f295222427803a7fc92b83386e5ec56,82d36ebbaaa026c713df2b7a47253efa,9c43759c41fe226a2702de300b9e580a,b7a2c1e4dd77f47605fdb33f4a2c2bdf,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b,c92ceeeeae88c8288176cbfd00c75e17,ce4c057e0a625bc9e64301a0cca1e206,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5</data>
      <data key="d11">0f3d5490cebe49efa2abbc42cc48ce13</data>
      <data key="d12">117</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="CIRUG&#205;A DIGESTIVA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutrici&#243;n enteral is recommended for patients undergoing cirug&#237;a digestiva when the gastrointestinal tract is functioning</data>
      <data key="d10">3dfc700a2eaec232c05b0a53f2089229</data>
      <data key="d11">5aff6e8e388443cd93678d134b12298e</data>
      <data key="d12">118</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="PANCREATITIS AGUDA">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL is an essential component in the management of patients suffering from PANCREATITIS AGUDA. Enteral nutrition serves as a treatment option, particularly for those with more severe forms of acute pancreatitis. It is utilized as nutritional support to enhance the clinical outcomes of these patients, thereby playing a critical role in their recovery and overall health management.</data>
      <data key="d10">57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009,5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d,88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e</data>
      <data key="d11">a78f1c7fd4464bbf87fb13280ad250e2</data>
      <data key="d12">119</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL (NE)">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support through enteral means is critical for managing patients with acute pancreatitis</data>
      <data key="d10">57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009</data>
      <data key="d11">a069a189ea0e4e65b67c44cd27dae8e7</data>
      <data key="d12">120</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL and NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL are two forms of nutritional support used in medical settings. NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL is primarily utilized for patients suffering from severe pancreatitis, as it is the preferred method of providing nutrition in such cases. On the other hand, NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is considered when NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL is not tolerable for the patient. Additionally, there is a possibility for nutritional support to transition from NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL to NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL as patients adapt to their treatment and their condition improves.</data>
      <data key="d10">5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe</data>
      <data key="d11">75534d0eb1704882ab47dcc6c0532856</data>
      <data key="d12">121</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="APACHE II">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Una puntuaci&#243;n mayor o igual a 10 en el &#237;ndice APACHE II indica que los pacientes son candidatos para recibir nutrici&#243;n enteral.</data>
      <data key="d10">5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d</data>
      <data key="d11">3d88e2ba89cd43da9149180330a59f1d</data>
      <data key="d12">122</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="CRITERIOS DE RANSON">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La presencia de al menos 3 criterios de Ranson en pacientes con pancreatitis grave sugiere que la nutrici&#243;n enteral puede influir en la evoluci&#243;n cl&#237;nica.</data>
      <data key="d10">5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d</data>
      <data key="d11">4e8f8e06d07345d7a05b12212c2c4699</data>
      <data key="d12">123</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="UCI">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral se administra a menudo en la UCI para pacientes con pancreatitis grave para mejorar su evoluci&#243;n cl&#237;nica.</data>
      <data key="d10">5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d</data>
      <data key="d11">ee91c2c0a2f74fd999a36f2e945b85f1</data>
      <data key="d12">124</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="SONDA ENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La sonda enteral es el medio a trav&#233;s del cual se administra la nutrici&#243;n enteral a los pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d</data>
      <data key="d11">23726d8c73894d45852fa094ee881108</data>
      <data key="d12">125</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="GASTROSTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La gastrostom&#237;a se utiliza para facilitar la nutrici&#243;n enteral en pacientes que no pueden alimentarse por v&#237;a oral.</data>
      <data key="d10">7469cc60475806b519e91abe2796aead</data>
      <data key="d11">9eef89a0814e4ebf81e696afbbee17f6</data>
      <data key="d12">126</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="PATIENT">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The patient receives enteral nutrition through a gastrostomy to meet his dietary requirements</data>
      <data key="d10">84e91b50850bfa0ad0122cdebf477a1d</data>
      <data key="d11">07da9a2a061e4d8b9b87182acfbcf3a1</data>
      <data key="d12">127</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE SAN JUAN">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enteral nutrition was provided to the patient during her stay at the Hospital Universitario de San Juan</data>
      <data key="d10">bc381304b682e075c7356c6edbfb0c2d</data>
      <data key="d11">0d1334942e7047a499fcde84fb827ed6</data>
      <data key="d12">128</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="FLUIDOTERAPIA ENDOVENOSA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The patient received both enteral nutrition and intravenous fluid therapy as part of her treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">bc381304b682e075c7356c6edbfb0c2d</data>
      <data key="d11">a52fac9f9a1345158f3699aa329f14e2</data>
      <data key="d12">129</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="ESPEN">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN recommends enteral nutrition as a method to improve intestinal adaptation</data>
      <data key="d10">896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe</data>
      <data key="d11">2785e03ac15549528b48dc420247721a</data>
      <data key="d12">130</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La diabetes mellitus tipo 2 requiere un ajuste cuidadoso de la nutrici&#243;n enteral para controlar los niveles de glucosa en sangre</data>
      <data key="d10">e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d11">3d73905c0adc4528b87d2909d82d95f5</data>
      <data key="d12">131</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="SUPLEMENTOS NUTRICIONALES ORALES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral puede complementarse con suplementos nutricionales orales para cubrir los requerimientos del paciente</data>
      <data key="d10">e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d11">21138001f43841a4954b84011f082ab0</data>
      <data key="d12">132</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="PEG">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral se implementa a trav&#233;s de la colocaci&#243;n de una gastrostom&#237;a percut&#225;nea endosc&#243;pica (PEG) para asegurar la ingesta adecuada de nutrientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">9c43759c41fe226a2702de300b9e580a</data>
      <data key="d11">b67ebb9495e84030a0893dd983c5cca3</data>
