    <edge source="DIABETES" target="HYPERGLYCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes is a chronic condition that frequently results in hyperglycemia, a state of elevated blood glucose levels. This relationship necessitates specific nutritional interventions to manage blood sugar levels effectively. Hyperglycemia is a common complication experienced by patients with diabetes, and its severity can be further exacerbated by conditions such as pancreatitis. Therefore, understanding the interplay between diabetes and hyperglycemia is crucial for effective management and treatment strategies.</data>
      <data key="d10">178140d0d29364593546d7d21393f2c6,e36c9b09870e14d19aa6eb7c82514499</data>
