    </edge>
    <edge source="DUODENOPANCREATECTOM&#205;A" target="CARCINOMA MUCINOSO DE P&#193;NCREAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Duodenopancreatectomy is a surgical treatment for mucinous pancreatic carcinoma, which can lead to complications such as diabetes and malabsorption.</data>
      <data key="d10">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d11">dd2dd40921ea4abf8e05e6a4d6906b79</data>
      <data key="d12">715</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MELAS" target="ACIDOSIS L&#193;CTICA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MELAS, which stands for Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes, is a condition characterized by a range of metabolic issues, one of the most significant being acidosis l&#225;ctica. Acidosis l&#225;ctica is a common metabolic issue in patients with MELAS, indicating a serious health concern. It is not only prevalent among these patients but also serves as a key diagnostic criterion for the condition. This highlights the critical relationship between MELAS and acidosis l&#225;ctica, underscoring the importance of monitoring and addressing this metabolic complication in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d11">b30e29816e034db5af1d7c7299d855e1</data>
      <data key="d12">716</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MELAS" target="EPILESIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Epilepsy is a significant neurological manifestation in MELAS, affecting a large percentage of patients</data>
      <data key="d10">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d11">760a3ba461bd41edb5ba640b4befb596</data>
      <data key="d12">717</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MELAS" target="NEUROPAT&#205;A PERIF&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Neuropat&#237;a perif&#233;rica is one of the neurological symptoms observed in MELAS patients</data>
      <data key="d10">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d11">8af5a74dde514ceaa4e51f539f59bcbc</data>
      <data key="d12">718</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MELAS" target="ARGININA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MELAS, a mitochondrial disorder, is associated with various vascular pathologies, and Arginina plays a significant role in this context. Arginina is involved in the production of nitric oxide, a vital molecule that contributes to vascular health. By increasing the availability of nitric oxide, Arginina is utilized as a therapeutic agent to potentially alleviate symptoms of MELAS, highlighting its importance in managing the condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d11">ed94643d1ce14a13a6523f7f4e0fb377</data>
      <data key="d12">719</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MELAS" target="CITRULINA">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MELAS, a mitochondrial disorder, is associated with various metabolic dysfunctions. Citrulina, a compound that acts as a precursor to nitric oxide, plays a relevant role in the context of MELAS pathology. It may enhance nitric oxide production, which could potentially be beneficial for patients suffering from MELAS. However, the specific effects of Citrulina on MELAS are not well-studied, indicating a need for further research to fully understand its implications in this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d11">bee192f1a1e049da9f3732cc7cfeb451</data>
      <data key="d12">720</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MELAS" target="CITOCROMO C">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Citocromo C interacts with nitric oxide and is implicated in the pathophysiology of MELAS</data>
      <data key="d10">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d11">57ade0118a844b1fa3505f5e139351a5</data>
      <data key="d12">721</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MELAS" target="HIPOACUSIA NEUROSENSORIAL">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MELAS, a mitochondrial disorder, is associated with various neurological symptoms, one of which is HIPOACUSIA NEUROSENSORIAL. This condition can significantly impact auditory function in patients with MELAS, making it a prevalent auditory symptom linked to the disorder.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d11">c325f249720d4a8a9d75156284814c07</data>
      <data key="d12">722</data>
      <data key="d13">0</data>
    </edge>
